 I was disputing that?", "tokens": [50720, 12555, 391, 14783, 11, 1338, 13, 1436, 291, 434, 4258, 1953, 11, 1699, 11, 437, 498, 286, 390, 37669, 278, 300, 30, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11058176944130345, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639264634906056e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 5492, "start": 66.64, "end": 68.8, "text": " Yes. What if the work was terrible?", "tokens": [50951, 1079, 13, 708, 498, 264, 589, 390, 6237, 30, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11058176944130345, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639264634906056e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 5492, "start": 69.22, "end": 76.76, "text": " Or what if that specific money in your checking account was earmarked for rent tomorrow?", "tokens": [51080, 1610, 437, 498, 300, 2685, 1460, 294, 428, 8568, 2696, 390, 1273, 5638, 292, 337, 6214, 4153, 30, 51457], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11058176944130345, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639264634906056e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 5492, "start": 76.8, "end": 79.46000000000001, "text": " Right. The AI has no idea about that context.", "tokens": [51459, 1779, 13, 440, 7318, 575, 572, 1558, 466, 300, 4319, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11058176944130345, "compression_ratio": 1.559670781893004, "no_speech_prob": 1.2639264634906056e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 7946, "start": 79.46, "end": 86.82, "text": " It doesn't. You feel that panic because instinctively you understand this fundamental truth about the messy real world.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 13, 509, 841, 300, 14783, 570, 16556, 3413, 291, 1223, 341, 8088, 3494, 466, 264, 16191, 957, 1002, 13, 50733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058991191151377916, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.477665646093529e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 7946, "start": 86.91999999999999, "end": 91.91999999999999, "text": " Which is that just because you're technically allowed to do something doesn't mean you actually have the authority to do it.", "tokens": [50738, 3013, 307, 300, 445, 570, 291, 434, 12120, 4350, 281, 360, 746, 1177, 380, 914, 291, 767, 362, 264, 8281, 281, 360, 309, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058991191151377916, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.477665646093529e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 7946, "start": 91.94, "end": 94.25999999999999, "text": " Or the reason to do it right at that exact middle second.", "tokens": [50989, 1610, 264, 1778, 281, 360, 309, 558, 412, 300, 1900, 2808, 1150, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058991191151377916, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.477665646093529e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 7946, "start": 94.36, "end": 101.83999999999999, "text": " Exactly. And that distinction, that massive, really perilous gap between what a software system is permitted to do", "tokens": [51110, 7587, 13, 400, 300, 16844, 11, 300, 5994, 11, 534, 46118, 563, 7417, 1296, 437, 257, 4722, 1185, 307, 28658, 281, 360, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.058991191151377916, "compression_ratio": 1.6352941176470588, "no_speech_prob": 1.477665646093529e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10184, "start": 101.84, "end": 106.86, "text": " and what is actually warranted in reality that is the absolute frontier of technology right now.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 437, 307, 767, 16354, 292, 294, 4103, 300, 307, 264, 8236, 35853, 295, 2899, 558, 586, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12268456168796706, "compression_ratio": 1.453061224489796, "no_speech_prob": 1.733844946956442e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10184, "start": 106.96000000000001, "end": 109.10000000000001, "text": " And that's exactly why we're doing this deep dive today.", "tokens": [50621, 400, 300, 311, 2293, 983, 321, 434, 884, 341, 2452, 9192, 965, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12268456168796706, "compression_ratio": 1.453061224489796, "no_speech_prob": 1.733844946956442e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10184, "start": 109.22, "end": 114.32000000000001, "text": " We are looking at a really paradigm shifting 2026 paper by Flixian.", "tokens": [50734, 492, 366, 1237, 412, 257, 534, 24709, 17573, 945, 10880, 3035, 538, 3235, 970, 952, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12268456168796706, "compression_ratio": 1.453061224489796, "no_speech_prob": 1.733844946956442e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 10184, "start": 114.44, "end": 121.52000000000001, "text": " Yeah. The paper is titled, From Verification to Commitment, Histories, Repair Warrants, and Admissible Continuation in Agenic Systems.", "tokens": [50995, 865, 13, 440, 3035, 307, 19841, 11, 3358, 4281, 3774, 281, 3046, 270, 518, 11, 9038, 2083, 11, 3696, 1246, 343, 2284, 1719, 11, 293, 46292, 41073, 14674, 16073, 294, 316, 1766, 299, 27059, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12268456168796706, "compression_ratio": 1.453061224489796, "no_speech_prob": 1.733844946956442e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 12152, "start": 121.52, "end": 128.62, "text": " Quite a mouthful. But our mission here is to be your shortcut to understanding this cutting edge stuff.", "tokens": [50365, 20464, 257, 4525, 906, 13, 583, 527, 4447, 510, 307, 281, 312, 428, 24822, 281, 3701, 341, 6492, 4691, 1507, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10767435473065044, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984638742846946e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 12152, "start": 129.06, "end": 134.56, "text": " Because, you know, we're moving past the era of AI just sitting in a chat box writing poems.", "tokens": [50742, 1436, 11, 291, 458, 11, 321, 434, 2684, 1791, 264, 4249, 295, 7318, 445, 3798, 294, 257, 5081, 2424, 3579, 24014, 13, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10767435473065044, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984638742846946e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 12152, "start": 134.68, "end": 138.32, "text": " Oh, absolutely. We are deep into the era of agentic systems now.", "tokens": [51023, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 492, 366, 2452, 666, 264, 4249, 295, 9461, 299, 3652, 586, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10767435473065044, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984638742846946e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 12152, "start": 138.48, "end": 143.68, "text": " Right. AIs that actually use tools, spend real money, alter databases permanently.", "tokens": [51213, 1779, 13, 316, 6802, 300, 767, 764, 3873, 11, 3496, 957, 1460, 11, 11337, 22380, 24042, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10767435473065044, "compression_ratio": 1.5087719298245614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5984638742846946e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 14368, "start": 143.68, "end": 146.84, "text": " So we need to answer this really difficult question.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 321, 643, 281, 1867, 341, 534, 2252, 1168, 13, 50523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08201055250306061, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841322615311014e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 14368, "start": 147.68, "end": 154.88, "text": " How do we build an AI that knows when to act, when to fix its own worldview, and when to just stop and ask for help?", "tokens": [50565, 1012, 360, 321, 1322, 364, 7318, 300, 3255, 562, 281, 605, 11, 562, 281, 3191, 1080, 1065, 41141, 11, 293, 562, 281, 445, 1590, 293, 1029, 337, 854, 30, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08201055250306061, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841322615311014e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 14368, "start": 155.0, "end": 161.84, "text": " It's about keeping an AI's realization of what's possible from automatically turning into, you know, an irreversible actuality.", "tokens": [50931, 467, 311, 466, 5145, 364, 7318, 311, 25138, 295, 437, 311, 1944, 490, 6772, 6246, 666, 11, 291, 458, 11, 364, 16014, 840, 964, 3539, 507, 13, 51273], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08201055250306061, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841322615311014e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 14368, "start": 161.94, "end": 166.02, "text": " So let's unpack this. The paper starts by basically critiquing how we evaluate AI today, right?", "tokens": [51278, 407, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 440, 3035, 3719, 538, 1936, 3113, 3221, 278, 577, 321, 13059, 7318, 965, 11, 558, 30, 51482], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08201055250306061, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841322615311014e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 14368, "start": 166.04000000000002, "end": 167.96, "text": " Yeah. They call it the trap of the single output.", "tokens": [51483, 865, 13, 814, 818, 309, 264, 11487, 295, 264, 2167, 5598, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08201055250306061, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841322615311014e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 14368, "start": 168.12, "end": 169.44, "text": " The single output. Okay. Explain it.", "tokens": [51587, 440, 2167, 5598, 13, 1033, 13, 39574, 309, 13, 51653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08201055250306061, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841322615311014e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 14368, "start": 169.62, "end": 172.3, "text": " Well, think about how we've tested AI up until now.", "tokens": [51662, 1042, 11, 519, 466, 577, 321, 600, 8246, 7318, 493, 1826, 586, 13, 51796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08201055250306061, "compression_ratio": 1.6470588235294117, "no_speech_prob": 1.4841322615311014e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 17230, "start": 172.3, "end": 178.58, "text": " If you ask a language model a trivia question, and it outputs the correct factual sentence, we grade that AI is correct.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1029, 257, 2856, 2316, 257, 48770, 1168, 11, 293, 309, 23930, 264, 3006, 48029, 8174, 11, 321, 7204, 300, 7318, 307, 3006, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0905473353499073, "compression_ratio": 1.589655172413793, "no_speech_prob": 1.2064818545251543e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 17230, "start": 178.68, "end": 180.0, "text": " We give it a gold star and move on.", "tokens": [50684, 492, 976, 309, 257, 3821, 3543, 293, 1286, 322, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0905473353499073, "compression_ratio": 1.589655172413793, "no_speech_prob": 1.2064818545251543e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 17230, "start": 180.16000000000003, "end": 189.06, "text": " Right. But the moment you give an AI access to persistent data, to real-world tools, that entire framework just becomes dangerously obsolete.", "tokens": [50758, 1779, 13, 583, 264, 1623, 291, 976, 364, 7318, 2105, 281, 24315, 1412, 11, 281, 957, 12, 13217, 3873, 11, 300, 2302, 8388, 445, 3643, 4330, 5098, 46333, 13, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0905473353499073, "compression_ratio": 1.589655172413793, "no_speech_prob": 1.2064818545251543e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 17230, "start": 189.36, "end": 196.08, "text": " I think I see why. I mean, if an AI writes a bad poem, the next time I ask for a poem, it just starts from a blank slate.", "tokens": [51218, 286, 519, 286, 536, 983, 13, 286, 914, 11, 498, 364, 7318, 13657, 257, 1578, 13065, 11, 264, 958, 565, 286, 1029, 337, 257, 13065, 11, 309, 445, 3719, 490, 257, 8247, 39118, 13, 51554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0905473353499073, "compression_ratio": 1.589655172413793, "no_speech_prob": 1.2064818545251543e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 17230, "start": 196.38000000000002, "end": 198.12, "text": " Exactly. The environment hasn't changed.", "tokens": [51569, 7587, 13, 440, 2823, 6132, 380, 3105, 13, 51656], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0905473353499073, "compression_ratio": 1.589655172413793, "no_speech_prob": 1.2064818545251543e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 19812, "start": 198.12, "end": 206.84, "text": " But if an AI, like, deletes a file on my hard drive, the world is fundamentally different for whatever action it tries to take next.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 364, 7318, 11, 411, 11, 1103, 37996, 257, 3991, 322, 452, 1152, 3332, 11, 264, 1002, 307, 17879, 819, 337, 2035, 3069, 309, 9898, 281, 747, 958, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11937619562018408, "compression_ratio": 1.4142857142857144, "no_speech_prob": 1.3559908404459087e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 19812, "start": 207.04, "end": 214.62, "text": " The environment has permanently mutated. And to explain this, the paper brings in some foundational research by Mercado and Lamusio.", "tokens": [50811, 440, 2823, 575, 24042, 5839, 770, 13, 400, 281, 2903, 341, 11, 264, 3035, 5607, 294, 512, 32195, 2132, 538, 18897, 1573, 293, 18825, 301, 1004, 13, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11937619562018408, "compression_ratio": 1.4142857142857144, "no_speech_prob": 1.3559908404459087e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 19812, "start": 214.72, "end": 215.84, "text": " Okay. What did they figure out?", "tokens": [51195, 1033, 13, 708, 630, 436, 2573, 484, 30, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11937619562018408, "compression_ratio": 1.4142857142857144, "no_speech_prob": 1.3559908404459087e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 21584, "start": 215.84, "end": 223.3, "text": " They formalized this concept called STEDS. It stands for Stateful Tool-Enabled Agentic Deployments.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 9860, 1602, 341, 3410, 1219, 4904, 4731, 50, 13, 467, 7382, 337, 4533, 906, 15934, 12, 16257, 8909, 27174, 299, 1346, 2384, 1117, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1373942753054061, "compression_ratio": 1.7256637168141593, "no_speech_prob": 1.5182075431899311e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 21584, "start": 223.38, "end": 225.56, "text": " Stateful Tool-Enabled Agentic Deployments.", "tokens": [50742, 4533, 906, 15934, 12, 16257, 8909, 27174, 299, 1346, 2384, 1117, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1373942753054061, "compression_ratio": 1.7256637168141593, "no_speech_prob": 1.5182075431899311e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 21584, "start": 225.68, "end": 225.86, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50857, 1033, 13, 50866], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1373942753054061, "compression_ratio": 1.7256637168141593, "no_speech_prob": 1.5182075431899311e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 21584, "start": 226.28, "end": 231.14000000000001, "text": " The core insight there is that correctness no longer belongs to a single tool call.", "tokens": [50887, 440, 4965, 11269, 456, 307, 300, 3006, 1287, 572, 2854, 12953, 281, 257, 2167, 2290, 818, 13, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1373942753054061, "compression_ratio": 1.7256637168141593, "no_speech_prob": 1.5182075431899311e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 21584, "start": 231.4, "end": 231.66, "text": " Meaning?", "tokens": [51143, 19948, 30, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1373942753054061, "compression_ratio": 1.7256637168141593, "no_speech_prob": 1.5182075431899311e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 21584, "start": 231.8, "end": 239.38, "text": " Meaning if an AI agent executes a command, that command changes the state of the world, and that cascades into the next state and then the next one.", "tokens": [51163, 19948, 498, 364, 7318, 9461, 4454, 1819, 257, 5622, 11, 300, 5622, 2962, 264, 1785, 295, 264, 1002, 11, 293, 300, 3058, 66, 2977, 666, 264, 958, 1785, 293, 550, 264, 958, 472, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1373942753054061, "compression_ratio": 1.7256637168141593, "no_speech_prob": 1.5182075431899311e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 23938, "start": 239.38, "end": 248.35999999999999, "text": " So, evaluating a single output in that scenario is kind of like judging a chess player by just looking at one isolated move, right?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 27479, 257, 2167, 5598, 294, 300, 9005, 307, 733, 295, 411, 23587, 257, 24122, 4256, 538, 445, 1237, 412, 472, 14621, 1286, 11, 558, 30, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390876052971173, "compression_ratio": 1.638095238095238, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214473119545048e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 23938, "start": 248.38, "end": 249.01999999999998, "text": " Great analogy.", "tokens": [50815, 3769, 21663, 13, 50847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390876052971173, "compression_ratio": 1.638095238095238, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214473119545048e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 23938, "start": 249.22, "end": 252.78, "text": " Like if I just show you a picture of a chess board and say, hey, look, I moved my knife forward.", "tokens": [50857, 1743, 498, 286, 445, 855, 291, 257, 3036, 295, 257, 24122, 3150, 293, 584, 11, 4177, 11, 574, 11, 286, 4259, 452, 7976, 2128, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390876052971173, "compression_ratio": 1.638095238095238, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214473119545048e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 23938, "start": 252.98, "end": 254.48, "text": " Right. In a vacuum, that might look brilliant.", "tokens": [51045, 1779, 13, 682, 257, 14224, 11, 300, 1062, 574, 10248, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390876052971173, "compression_ratio": 1.638095238095238, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214473119545048e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 23938, "start": 254.72, "end": 257.82, "text": " Yeah. It's a legally permitted move. It looks aggressive.", "tokens": [51132, 865, 13, 467, 311, 257, 21106, 28658, 1286, 13, 467, 1542, 10762, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390876052971173, "compression_ratio": 1.638095238095238, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214473119545048e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 23938, "start": 258.54, "end": 264.14, "text": " But if you zoom out and look at the whole trajectory of the game, you might see I just walked right into a trap.", "tokens": [51323, 583, 498, 291, 8863, 484, 293, 574, 412, 264, 1379, 21512, 295, 264, 1216, 11, 291, 1062, 536, 286, 445, 7628, 558, 666, 257, 11487, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390876052971173, "compression_ratio": 1.638095238095238, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214473119545048e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 23938, "start": 264.21999999999997, "end": 266.86, "text": " A trap the opponent has been setting up for six turns.", "tokens": [51607, 316, 11487, 264, 10620, 575, 668, 3287, 493, 337, 2309, 4523, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11390876052971173, "compression_ratio": 1.638095238095238, "no_speech_prob": 1.7214473119545048e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 26686, "start": 266.86, "end": 271.92, "text": " Exactly. The history of the game completely dictates the meaning of that present action.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 2503, 295, 264, 1216, 2584, 12569, 1024, 264, 3620, 295, 300, 1974, 3069, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11115191964542165, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.324853421413863e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 26686, "start": 272.56, "end": 285.3, "text": " And Mercado and Lamutio prove mathematically that interface-level restraint, meaning just writing a simple rule that blocks an AI from making a forbidden move in the moment, that cannot guarantee system-level safety.", "tokens": [50650, 400, 18897, 1573, 293, 18825, 325, 1004, 7081, 44003, 300, 9226, 12, 12418, 49281, 11, 3620, 445, 3579, 257, 2199, 4978, 300, 8474, 364, 7318, 490, 1455, 257, 25990, 1286, 294, 264, 1623, 11, 300, 2644, 10815, 1185, 12, 12418, 4514, 13, 51287], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11115191964542165, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.324853421413863e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 26686, "start": 285.5, "end": 287.0, "text": " Because it's not looking at the whole board.", "tokens": [51297, 1436, 309, 311, 406, 1237, 412, 264, 1379, 3150, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11115191964542165, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.324853421413863e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 26686, "start": 287.08000000000004, "end": 295.64, "text": " Precisely. They map out these incredibly complex branching transition systems using something called first-order computation tree logic.", "tokens": [51376, 48746, 736, 13, 814, 4471, 484, 613, 6252, 3997, 9819, 278, 6034, 3652, 1228, 746, 1219, 700, 12, 4687, 24903, 4230, 9952, 13, 51804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11115191964542165, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.324853421413863e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 29564, "start": 295.64, "end": 301.68, "text": " Whoa. Okay. Hold on. First-order computation tree logic. Stop right there. In English, what are we actually talking about?", "tokens": [50365, 7521, 13, 1033, 13, 6962, 322, 13, 2386, 12, 4687, 24903, 4230, 9952, 13, 5535, 558, 456, 13, 682, 3669, 11, 437, 366, 321, 767, 1417, 466, 30, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09533403160866727, "compression_ratio": 1.5598290598290598, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 29564, "start": 301.9, "end": 305.08, "text": " Think of it as a mathematical map of a multiverse.", "tokens": [50678, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 257, 18894, 4471, 295, 257, 2120, 5376, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09533403160866727, "compression_ratio": 1.5598290598290598, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 29564, "start": 305.24, "end": 306.68, "text": " A multiverse. Okay. I'm listening.", "tokens": [50845, 316, 2120, 5376, 13, 1033, 13, 286, 478, 4764, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09533403160866727, "compression_ratio": 1.5598290598290598, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 29564, "start": 307.26, "end": 315.8, "text": " Instead of just looking at a straight line of past events, computation tree logic lets a computer analyze a branching tree of all possible future timelines.", "tokens": [50946, 7156, 295, 445, 1237, 412, 257, 2997, 1622, 295, 1791, 3931, 11, 24903, 4230, 9952, 6653, 257, 3820, 12477, 257, 9819, 278, 4230, 295, 439, 1944, 2027, 45886, 13, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09533403160866727, "compression_ratio": 1.5598290598290598, "no_speech_prob": 1.507358907831824e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 31580, "start": 315.8, "end": 319.08, "text": " So it's looking at every path that could result from the current state.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 309, 311, 1237, 412, 633, 3100, 300, 727, 1874, 490, 264, 2190, 1785, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09926696827537135, "compression_ratio": 1.4597156398104265, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349514836936808e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 31580, "start": 319.28000000000003, "end": 328.46000000000004, "text": " Right. It's a way for a system to verify if a specific safety rule holds true, not just right now, but across all reachable future paths.", "tokens": [50539, 1779, 13, 467, 311, 257, 636, 337, 257, 1185, 281, 16888, 498, 257, 2685, 4514, 4978, 9190, 2074, 11, 406, 445, 558, 586, 11, 457, 2108, 439, 2524, 712, 2027, 14518, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09926696827537135, "compression_ratio": 1.4597156398104265, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349514836936808e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 31580, "start": 328.86, "end": 336.02, "text": " Okay. So it is literally Dr. Strange looking at 14 million alternate futures to see if we survive.", "tokens": [51018, 1033, 13, 407, 309, 307, 3736, 2491, 13, 29068, 1237, 412, 3499, 2459, 18873, 26071, 281, 536, 498, 321, 7867, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09926696827537135, "compression_ratio": 1.4597156398104265, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349514836936808e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 33602, "start": 336.02, "end": 348.94, "text": " In a sense, yeah. But the terrifying takeaway from analyzing these systems is that a locally permissible call, a move that looks totally safe right now, might actually be participating in a globally defective history.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 257, 2020, 11, 1338, 13, 583, 264, 18106, 30681, 490, 23663, 613, 3652, 307, 300, 257, 16143, 4784, 41073, 818, 11, 257, 1286, 300, 1542, 3879, 3273, 558, 586, 11, 1062, 767, 312, 13950, 294, 257, 18958, 16445, 488, 2503, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09751107753851475, "compression_ratio": 1.5617021276595744, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993287865249338e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 33602, "start": 349.2, "end": 357.12, "text": " So just because you blocked one unsafe call, that doesn't mean the system is making any actual progress towards safely completing your task.", "tokens": [51024, 407, 445, 570, 291, 15470, 472, 35948, 818, 11, 300, 1177, 380, 914, 264, 1185, 307, 1455, 604, 3539, 4205, 3030, 11750, 19472, 428, 5633, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09751107753851475, "compression_ratio": 1.5617021276595744, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993287865249338e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 33602, "start": 357.24, "end": 357.84, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51426, 7587, 13, 51456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09751107753851475, "compression_ratio": 1.5617021276595744, "no_speech_prob": 1.3993287865249338e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 35784, "start": 357.84, "end": 361.73999999999995, "text": " Wow. You know, this makes so much sense of a frustration I hear from people all the time.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 509, 458, 11, 341, 1669, 370, 709, 2020, 295, 257, 20491, 286, 1568, 490, 561, 439, 264, 565, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 35784, "start": 361.88, "end": 362.34, "text": " Which is what?", "tokens": [50567, 3013, 307, 437, 30, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 35784, "start": 362.59999999999997, "end": 368.53999999999996, "text": " You're working with an AI, maybe having it organize a really complex spreadsheet or code a website.", "tokens": [50603, 509, 434, 1364, 365, 364, 7318, 11, 1310, 1419, 309, 13859, 257, 534, 3997, 27733, 420, 3089, 257, 3144, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 35784, "start": 368.73999999999995, "end": 370.12, "text": " Yeah, a multi-step task.", "tokens": [50910, 865, 11, 257, 4825, 12, 16792, 5633, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 35784, "start": 370.2, "end": 373.06, "text": " Right. And halfway through, it just seems to completely lose the plot.", "tokens": [50983, 1779, 13, 400, 15461, 807, 11, 309, 445, 2544, 281, 2584, 3624, 264, 7542, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 35784, "start": 373.35999999999996, "end": 380.12, "text": " It starts making suggestions that technically follow the immediate prompt, but they totally contradict the overall goal you've been working on for an hour.", "tokens": [51141, 467, 3719, 1455, 13396, 300, 12120, 1524, 264, 11629, 12391, 11, 457, 436, 3879, 28900, 264, 4787, 3387, 291, 600, 668, 1364, 322, 337, 364, 1773, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 35784, "start": 380.34, "end": 382.88, "text": " Yes. People always think that's just a memory issue.", "tokens": [51490, 1079, 13, 3432, 1009, 519, 300, 311, 445, 257, 4675, 2734, 13, 51617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 35784, "start": 383.2, "end": 383.88, "text": " It's not memory.", "tokens": [51633, 467, 311, 406, 4675, 13, 51667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11477483602670523, "compression_ratio": 1.6085626911314985, "no_speech_prob": 1.3408029027328627e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 38388, "start": 383.88, "end": 391.28, "text": " Not exactly. The AI just lacks a structural understanding of the evolving operational state. It doesn't see the trajectory.", "tokens": [50365, 1726, 2293, 13, 440, 7318, 445, 31132, 257, 15067, 3701, 295, 264, 21085, 16607, 1785, 13, 467, 1177, 380, 536, 264, 21512, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10618358280347741, "compression_ratio": 1.6533333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437449716644957e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 38388, "start": 391.52, "end": 392.36, "text": " That is wild.", "tokens": [50747, 663, 307, 4868, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10618358280347741, "compression_ratio": 1.6533333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437449716644957e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 38388, "start": 392.48, "end": 397.76, "text": " And the paper introduces a really deep concept to explain why AI struggles with this.", "tokens": [50795, 400, 264, 3035, 31472, 257, 534, 2452, 3410, 281, 2903, 983, 7318, 17592, 365, 341, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10618358280347741, "compression_ratio": 1.6533333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437449716644957e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 38388, "start": 398.0, "end": 400.88, "text": " It revolves around something called identifier equivariance.", "tokens": [51071, 467, 47934, 926, 746, 1219, 45690, 48726, 3504, 719, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10618358280347741, "compression_ratio": 1.6533333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437449716644957e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 38388, "start": 401.64, "end": 403.74, "text": " Identifier equivariance. Okay, break that down for me.", "tokens": [51253, 25905, 9902, 48726, 3504, 719, 13, 1033, 11, 1821, 300, 760, 337, 385, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10618358280347741, "compression_ratio": 1.6533333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437449716644957e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 38388, "start": 404.02, "end": 412.74, "text": " Well, we naturally assume we can just build a universal external judge, like a separate AI that just watches the main AI and says, yep, that action is safe.", "tokens": [51372, 1042, 11, 321, 8195, 6552, 321, 393, 445, 1322, 257, 11455, 8320, 6995, 11, 411, 257, 4994, 7318, 300, 445, 17062, 264, 2135, 7318, 293, 1619, 11, 18633, 11, 300, 3069, 307, 3273, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10618358280347741, "compression_ratio": 1.6533333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.4437449716644957e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 41274, "start": 412.74, "end": 414.14, "text": " Right, like an AI supervisor.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 411, 364, 7318, 24610, 13, 50435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11508176567849149, "compression_ratio": 1.5101214574898785, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266134931370522e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 41274, "start": 414.40000000000003, "end": 421.02, "text": " But mathematically unrestricted verification of a live changing system is undecidable. It's actually a fantasy.", "tokens": [50448, 583, 44003, 35103, 3740, 292, 30206, 295, 257, 1621, 4473, 1185, 307, 674, 3045, 38089, 13, 467, 311, 767, 257, 13861, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11508176567849149, "compression_ratio": 1.5101214574898785, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266134931370522e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 41274, "start": 421.2, "end": 426.62, "text": " Why is it a fantasy? If we know the rules, why can't a monitor just enforce them?", "tokens": [50788, 1545, 307, 309, 257, 13861, 30, 759, 321, 458, 264, 4474, 11, 983, 393, 380, 257, 6002, 445, 24825, 552, 30, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11508176567849149, "compression_ratio": 1.5101214574898785, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266134931370522e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 41274, "start": 426.7, "end": 433.48, "text": " Because of how an AI fundamentally understands the world through its internal representations. Let's ground this in a real world scenario.", "tokens": [51063, 1436, 295, 577, 364, 7318, 17879, 15146, 264, 1002, 807, 1080, 6920, 33358, 13, 961, 311, 2727, 341, 294, 257, 957, 1002, 9005, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11508176567849149, "compression_ratio": 1.5101214574898785, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266134931370522e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 41274, "start": 433.6, "end": 434.06, "text": " Please do.", "tokens": [51408, 2555, 360, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11508176567849149, "compression_ratio": 1.5101214574898785, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266134931370522e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 43406, "start": 434.06, "end": 437.82, "text": " Imagine an AI managing a hospital's patient database.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 364, 7318, 11642, 257, 4530, 311, 4537, 8149, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367917216101358, "compression_ratio": 1.6180257510729614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251286561782096e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 43406, "start": 438.0, "end": 438.16, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50562, 1033, 13, 50570], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367917216101358, "compression_ratio": 1.6180257510729614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251286561782096e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 43406, "start": 438.38, "end": 442.92, "text": " You have two database states that to the AI's internal math are completely identical.", "tokens": [50581, 509, 362, 732, 8149, 4368, 300, 281, 264, 7318, 311, 6920, 5221, 366, 2584, 14800, 13, 50808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367917216101358, "compression_ratio": 1.6180257510729614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251286561782096e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 43406, "start": 443.56, "end": 450.58, "text": " The only difference is that the opaque identifiers, the random string of numbers representing patient A and patient B, have been swapped.", "tokens": [50840, 440, 787, 2649, 307, 300, 264, 42687, 2473, 23463, 11, 264, 4974, 6798, 295, 3547, 13460, 4537, 316, 293, 4537, 363, 11, 362, 668, 50011, 13, 51191], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367917216101358, "compression_ratio": 1.6180257510729614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251286561782096e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 43406, "start": 450.8, "end": 455.38, "text": " So the system looks exactly the same to the AI, just with different name tags on the folders.", "tokens": [51202, 407, 264, 1185, 1542, 2293, 264, 912, 281, 264, 7318, 11, 445, 365, 819, 1315, 18632, 322, 264, 31082, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12367917216101358, "compression_ratio": 1.6180257510729614, "no_speech_prob": 1.5251286561782096e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 45538, "start": 455.38, "end": 468.38, "text": " Exactly. Now, if the AI selects the exact same corresponding actions under that renaming, say, ordering the same blood test for the newly swapped IDs, the representations are operationally interchangeable.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 823, 11, 498, 264, 7318, 3048, 82, 264, 1900, 912, 11760, 5909, 833, 300, 8124, 5184, 11, 584, 11, 21739, 264, 912, 3390, 1500, 337, 264, 15109, 50011, 48212, 11, 264, 33358, 366, 6916, 379, 30358, 712, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09021924601660834, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941365844902467e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 45538, "start": 469.14, "end": 470.08, "text": " Okay, that makes sense.", "tokens": [51053, 1033, 11, 300, 1669, 2020, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09021924601660834, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941365844902467e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 45538, "start": 470.24, "end": 475.08, "text": " But if it doesn't, their apparent structural equivalence fails at the level of intervention.", "tokens": [51108, 583, 498, 309, 1177, 380, 11, 641, 18335, 15067, 9052, 655, 18199, 412, 264, 1496, 295, 13176, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09021924601660834, "compression_ratio": 1.5188679245283019, "no_speech_prob": 1.6941365844902467e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 47508, "start": 475.08, "end": 482.41999999999996, "text": " The paper explicitly warns that observational equivalence does not equal intervention-preserving equivalence.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 20803, 12286, 82, 300, 9951, 1478, 9052, 655, 775, 406, 2681, 13176, 12, 14508, 20186, 9052, 655, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1062392672976932, "compression_ratio": 1.7016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511919447900533e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 47508, "start": 482.59999999999997, "end": 484.0, "text": " Let me make sure I'm tracking this.", "tokens": [50741, 961, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 11603, 341, 13, 50811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1062392672976932, "compression_ratio": 1.7016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511919447900533e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 47508, "start": 484.34, "end": 494.06, "text": " Just because two hospital records look structurally identical to the AI's internal math, that doesn't mean taking the same action will produce the same safe result in the real world.", "tokens": [50828, 1449, 570, 732, 4530, 7724, 574, 6594, 6512, 14800, 281, 264, 7318, 311, 6920, 5221, 11, 300, 1177, 380, 914, 1940, 264, 912, 3069, 486, 5258, 264, 912, 3273, 1874, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1062392672976932, "compression_ratio": 1.7016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511919447900533e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 47508, "start": 494.24, "end": 494.88, "text": " Spot on.", "tokens": [51323, 19102, 322, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1062392672976932, "compression_ratio": 1.7016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511919447900533e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 47508, "start": 494.94, "end": 502.28, "text": " Because, I mean, patient A might have a severe allergy that just isn't captured in that specific structural representation the AI is using to judge the equivalence.", "tokens": [51358, 1436, 11, 286, 914, 11, 4537, 316, 1062, 362, 257, 8922, 41505, 300, 445, 1943, 380, 11828, 294, 300, 2685, 15067, 10290, 264, 7318, 307, 1228, 281, 6995, 264, 9052, 655, 13, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1062392672976932, "compression_ratio": 1.7016949152542373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3511919447900533e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 50228, "start": 502.28, "end": 510.91999999999996, "text": " Yes. The AI has to respect the actual symmetries of the system it's acting upon, not just its internal representation of those symmetries.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 440, 7318, 575, 281, 3104, 264, 3539, 14232, 302, 2244, 295, 264, 1185, 309, 311, 6577, 3564, 11, 406, 445, 1080, 6920, 10290, 295, 729, 14232, 302, 2244, 13, 50797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08952321043801964, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.666132722581316e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 50228, "start": 511.21999999999997, "end": 521.9, "text": " Wow. So if the AI's understanding of the environment isn't structurally sound across time, the whole idea of let's just verify every single step completely falls apart.", "tokens": [50812, 3153, 13, 407, 498, 264, 7318, 311, 3701, 295, 264, 2823, 1943, 380, 6594, 6512, 1626, 2108, 565, 11, 264, 1379, 1558, 295, 718, 311, 445, 16888, 633, 2167, 1823, 2584, 8804, 4936, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08952321043801964, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.666132722581316e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 50228, "start": 522.0, "end": 522.9599999999999, "text": " It totally collapses.", "tokens": [51351, 467, 3879, 48765, 13, 51399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08952321043801964, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.666132722581316e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 50228, "start": 523.4399999999999, "end": 528.26, "text": " Which brings us to the main architectural proposal of this paper, CLIO.", "tokens": [51423, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 2135, 26621, 11494, 295, 341, 3035, 11, 12855, 15167, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08952321043801964, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.666132722581316e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 50228, "start": 528.52, "end": 530.8399999999999, "text": " CLIO. Okay, so what is CLIO doing differently?", "tokens": [51677, 12855, 15167, 13, 1033, 11, 370, 437, 307, 12855, 15167, 884, 7614, 30, 51793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08952321043801964, "compression_ratio": 1.5830388692579505, "no_speech_prob": 2.666132722581316e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 53084, "start": 530.84, "end": 537.96, "text": " The authors describe CLIO not as a new detector and not as a new verifier, but as a coordination layer.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16552, 6786, 12855, 15167, 406, 382, 257, 777, 25712, 293, 406, 382, 257, 777, 1306, 9902, 11, 457, 382, 257, 21252, 4583, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047003625666053, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321926007619505e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 53084, "start": 538.2, "end": 538.96, "text": " A coordination layer.", "tokens": [50733, 316, 21252, 4583, 13, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047003625666053, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321926007619505e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 53084, "start": 539.0600000000001, "end": 546.34, "text": " Yeah. It completely deconstructs how an AI takes action by splitting the process into five distinct separate objects.", "tokens": [50776, 865, 13, 467, 2584, 49473, 1757, 82, 577, 364, 7318, 2516, 3069, 538, 30348, 264, 1399, 666, 1732, 10644, 4994, 6565, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047003625666053, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321926007619505e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 53084, "start": 546.5, "end": 547.46, "text": " Where are the five objects?", "tokens": [51148, 2305, 366, 264, 1732, 6565, 30, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047003625666053, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321926007619505e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 53084, "start": 547.6600000000001, "end": 554.38, "text": " You have retained history, diagnosis, admissible continuations, proposed repair, and explicit commitment.", "tokens": [51206, 509, 362, 33438, 2503, 11, 15217, 11, 5910, 41073, 2993, 763, 11, 10348, 10535, 11, 293, 13691, 8371, 13, 51542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047003625666053, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321926007619505e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 53084, "start": 554.58, "end": 557.94, "text": " Okay. History, diagnosis, continuations, repair, and commitment.", "tokens": [51552, 1033, 13, 12486, 11, 15217, 11, 2993, 763, 11, 10535, 11, 293, 8371, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09047003625666053, "compression_ratio": 1.7333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8321926007619505e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 55794, "start": 557.94, "end": 564.3800000000001, "text": " Right. But the genius of CLIO isn't just that these five components exist, it's the intentional gaps between them.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 583, 264, 14017, 295, 12855, 15167, 1943, 380, 445, 300, 613, 1732, 6677, 2514, 11, 309, 311, 264, 21935, 15031, 1296, 552, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1072043776512146, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.875642002824307e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 55794, "start": 564.46, "end": 565.0600000000001, "text": " The gaps.", "tokens": [50691, 440, 15031, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1072043776512146, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.875642002824307e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 55794, "start": 565.2, "end": 567.8800000000001, "text": " The paper refers to these as non-implications.", "tokens": [50728, 440, 3035, 14942, 281, 613, 382, 2107, 12, 332, 4770, 763, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1072043776512146, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.875642002824307e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 55794, "start": 568.0600000000001, "end": 573.0, "text": " I want to push back on this a little, or at least, you know, channel the frustration of every software engineer listening to this right now.", "tokens": [50871, 286, 528, 281, 2944, 646, 322, 341, 257, 707, 11, 420, 412, 1935, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2269, 264, 20491, 295, 633, 4722, 11403, 4764, 281, 341, 558, 586, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1072043776512146, "compression_ratio": 1.471698113207547, "no_speech_prob": 1.875642002824307e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 57300, "start": 573.0, "end": 582.88, "text": " If we give the AI a history, and it successfully forms a diagnosis that something is wrong, why doesn't that automatically mean it should initiate a repair?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 321, 976, 264, 7318, 257, 2503, 11, 293, 309, 10727, 6422, 257, 15217, 300, 746, 307, 2085, 11, 983, 1177, 380, 300, 6772, 914, 309, 820, 31574, 257, 10535, 30, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12326103601700221, "compression_ratio": 1.4752475247524752, "no_speech_prob": 1.6809622270519409e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 57300, "start": 583.04, "end": 583.86, "text": " That's the trap.", "tokens": [50867, 663, 311, 264, 11487, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12326103601700221, "compression_ratio": 1.4752475247524752, "no_speech_prob": 1.6809622270519409e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 57300, "start": 584.2, "end": 590.44, "text": " And if we have a list of admissible continuations, like safe next steps, why don't we just let the AI pick one and go?", "tokens": [50925, 400, 498, 321, 362, 257, 1329, 295, 5910, 41073, 2993, 763, 11, 411, 3273, 958, 4439, 11, 983, 500, 380, 321, 445, 718, 264, 7318, 1888, 472, 293, 352, 30, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12326103601700221, "compression_ratio": 1.4752475247524752, "no_speech_prob": 1.6809622270519409e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 57300, "start": 590.66, "end": 590.88, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51248, 865, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12326103601700221, "compression_ratio": 1.4752475247524752, "no_speech_prob": 1.6809622270519409e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 59088, "start": 590.88, "end": 596.68, "text": " Isn't this coordination layer just adding a massive amount of bureaucratic red tape to an autonomous agent?", "tokens": [50365, 6998, 380, 341, 21252, 4583, 445, 5127, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 26360, 25198, 2182, 7314, 281, 364, 23797, 9461, 30, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08492590056525337, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758222193089979e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 59088, "start": 596.82, "end": 598.12, "text": " It looks like red tape, sure.", "tokens": [50662, 467, 1542, 411, 2182, 7314, 11, 988, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08492590056525337, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758222193089979e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 59088, "start": 598.68, "end": 603.08, "text": " I mean, if I'm paying for an autonomous agent, I want it to be fast, decisive, and efficient, right?", "tokens": [50755, 286, 914, 11, 498, 286, 478, 6229, 337, 364, 23797, 9461, 11, 286, 528, 309, 281, 312, 2370, 11, 34998, 11, 293, 7148, 11, 558, 30, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08492590056525337, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758222193089979e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 59088, "start": 603.24, "end": 610.58, "text": " And that instinct to optimize for speed and seamless execution is exactly what has led to so many agentic failures.", "tokens": [50983, 400, 300, 16556, 281, 19719, 337, 3073, 293, 28677, 15058, 307, 2293, 437, 575, 4684, 281, 370, 867, 9461, 299, 20774, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08492590056525337, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758222193089979e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 59088, "start": 610.84, "end": 611.22, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [51363, 4083, 30, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08492590056525337, "compression_ratio": 1.5807860262008733, "no_speech_prob": 1.7758222193089979e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 61122, "start": 611.22, "end": 611.6600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 61122, "start": 612.24, "end": 615.44, "text": " That bureaucratic red tape is the literal architecture of safety.", "tokens": [50416, 663, 26360, 25198, 2182, 7314, 307, 264, 20411, 9482, 295, 4514, 13, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 61122, "start": 616.2, "end": 620.5600000000001, "text": " The paper centers on a concept called the admissible but non-committable proposition.", "tokens": [50614, 440, 3035, 10898, 322, 257, 3410, 1219, 264, 5910, 41073, 457, 2107, 12, 13278, 593, 712, 24830, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 61122, "start": 620.94, "end": 622.08, "text": " Admissible but non-committable.", "tokens": [50851, 46292, 41073, 457, 2107, 12, 13278, 593, 712, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 61122, "start": 622.2, "end": 624.24, "text": " Okay, let's look at the logic of those gaps you mentioned.", "tokens": [50914, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 9952, 295, 729, 15031, 291, 2835, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 61122, "start": 624.34, "end": 624.5600000000001, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51021, 4894, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 61122, "start": 624.8000000000001, "end": 627.6600000000001, "text": " A system might accumulate a massive amount of history, right?", "tokens": [51044, 316, 1185, 1062, 33384, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 2503, 11, 558, 30, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 61122, "start": 628.02, "end": 632.86, "text": " But that history might still be insufficient to actually form a reliable diagnosis of a problem.", "tokens": [51205, 583, 300, 2503, 1062, 920, 312, 41709, 281, 767, 1254, 257, 12924, 15217, 295, 257, 1154, 13, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 61122, "start": 633.1, "end": 640.08, "text": " Meaning it knows something is weird, but it doesn't have quite enough data to label the specific disease.", "tokens": [51459, 19948, 309, 3255, 746, 307, 3657, 11, 457, 309, 1177, 380, 362, 1596, 1547, 1412, 281, 7645, 264, 2685, 4752, 13, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 61122, "start": 640.34, "end": 640.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51821, 7587, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13320200993464543, "compression_ratio": 1.652037617554859, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191783378151746e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 64122, "start": 641.5400000000001, "end": 649.08, "text": " Moving to the next gap, the system might actually successfully detect a failure, it has a clear diagnosis,", "tokens": [50381, 14242, 281, 264, 958, 7417, 11, 264, 1185, 1062, 767, 10727, 5531, 257, 7763, 11, 309, 575, 257, 1850, 15217, 11, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625490577853456, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906250263267532e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 64122, "start": 649.64, "end": 654.0600000000001, "text": " without being able to identify any admissible repair within its constraints.", "tokens": [50786, 1553, 885, 1075, 281, 5876, 604, 5910, 41073, 10535, 1951, 1080, 18491, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625490577853456, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906250263267532e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 64122, "start": 654.24, "end": 657.1, "text": " So it knows what's broken, but doesn't know a safe way to fix it.", "tokens": [51016, 407, 309, 3255, 437, 311, 5463, 11, 457, 1177, 380, 458, 257, 3273, 636, 281, 3191, 309, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625490577853456, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906250263267532e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 64122, "start": 657.1800000000001, "end": 657.4200000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51163, 1779, 13, 51175], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625490577853456, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906250263267532e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 64122, "start": 657.74, "end": 662.0400000000001, "text": " And most importantly, it might validate a proposed repair as technically safe", "tokens": [51191, 400, 881, 8906, 11, 309, 1062, 29562, 257, 10348, 10535, 382, 12120, 3273, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625490577853456, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906250263267532e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 64122, "start": 662.0400000000001, "end": 667.34, "text": " without having the authority to actually commit that repair to the live state of the world.", "tokens": [51406, 1553, 1419, 264, 8281, 281, 767, 5599, 300, 10535, 281, 264, 1621, 1785, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 51671], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1625490577853456, "compression_ratio": 1.632183908045977, "no_speech_prob": 1.8906250263267532e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 66734, "start": 667.34, "end": 671.24, "text": " Oh, so going all the way back to my bank account example from the beginning.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 370, 516, 439, 264, 636, 646, 281, 452, 3765, 2696, 1365, 490, 264, 2863, 13, 50560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21020320256551106, "compression_ratio": 1.4110429447852761, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881657747061518e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 66734, "start": 671.36, "end": 672.46, "text": " Yes, perfect example.", "tokens": [50566, 1079, 11, 2176, 1365, 13, 50621], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21020320256551106, "compression_ratio": 1.4110429447852761, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881657747061518e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 66734, "start": 672.6800000000001, "end": 674.6600000000001, "text": " Paying that invoice was an admissible continuation.", "tokens": [50632, 11431, 278, 300, 47919, 390, 364, 5910, 41073, 29357, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21020320256551106, "compression_ratio": 1.4110429447852761, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881657747061518e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 66734, "start": 675.4200000000001, "end": 677.76, "text": " It didn't violate any laws of banking or mathematics.", "tokens": [50769, 467, 994, 380, 37478, 604, 6064, 295, 18261, 420, 18666, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21020320256551106, "compression_ratio": 1.4110429447852761, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881657747061518e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 66734, "start": 677.9, "end": 679.0400000000001, "text": " It was technically sound.", "tokens": [50893, 467, 390, 12120, 1626, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21020320256551106, "compression_ratio": 1.4110429447852761, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881657747061518e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 67904, "start": 679.04, "end": 686.0799999999999, "text": " But it was a non-committable proposition because the AI lacked the specific warrant for me to execute it in reality.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 390, 257, 2107, 12, 13278, 593, 712, 24830, 570, 264, 7318, 41481, 264, 2685, 16354, 337, 385, 281, 14483, 309, 294, 4103, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375605889729091, "compression_ratio": 1.4026845637583893, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956364055226934e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 67904, "start": 686.18, "end": 686.52, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50722, 7587, 13, 50739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375605889729091, "compression_ratio": 1.4026845637583893, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956364055226934e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 67904, "start": 687.16, "end": 689.9399999999999, "text": " Verification is just a restriction on what is possible.", "tokens": [50771, 4281, 3774, 307, 445, 257, 29529, 322, 437, 307, 1944, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375605889729091, "compression_ratio": 1.4026845637583893, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956364055226934e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 67904, "start": 690.06, "end": 691.4, "text": " It is not a license to act.", "tokens": [50916, 467, 307, 406, 257, 10476, 281, 605, 13, 50983], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1375605889729091, "compression_ratio": 1.4026845637583893, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956364055226934e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 69140, "start": 691.4, "end": 691.8, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20908579459557167, "compression_ratio": 1.3466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.585302744112893e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 69140, "start": 692.4599999999999, "end": 693.56, "text": " That's a huge distinction.", "tokens": [50418, 663, 311, 257, 2603, 16844, 13, 50473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20908579459557167, "compression_ratio": 1.3466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.585302744112893e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 69140, "start": 693.88, "end": 697.48, "text": " The mathematics of the paper define this very rigidly in equation 14.", "tokens": [50489, 440, 18666, 295, 264, 3035, 6964, 341, 588, 22195, 356, 294, 5367, 3499, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20908579459557167, "compression_ratio": 1.3466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.585302744112893e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 69140, "start": 698.04, "end": 702.76, "text": " It basically states that just because a repair is admissible given the history, the operative state,", "tokens": [50697, 467, 1936, 4368, 300, 445, 570, 257, 10535, 307, 5910, 41073, 2212, 264, 2503, 11, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 11, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20908579459557167, "compression_ratio": 1.3466666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.585302744112893e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 70276, "start": 702.76, "end": 708.6, "text": " and the diagnosis that does not mathematically imply there exists a committed transition to a new state.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 264, 15217, 300, 775, 406, 44003, 33616, 456, 8198, 257, 7784, 6034, 281, 257, 777, 1785, 13, 50657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508056905009959, "compression_ratio": 1.5735849056603775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8679196644305618e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 70276, "start": 708.92, "end": 713.3199999999999, "text": " Verification just establishes membership in a permitted region of actions.", "tokens": [50673, 4281, 3774, 445, 8327, 279, 16560, 294, 257, 28658, 4458, 295, 5909, 13, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508056905009959, "compression_ratio": 1.5735849056603775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8679196644305618e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 70276, "start": 714.08, "end": 717.5, "text": " It cannot manufacture the authority to actually change the world.", "tokens": [50931, 467, 2644, 27400, 264, 8281, 281, 767, 1319, 264, 1002, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508056905009959, "compression_ratio": 1.5735849056603775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8679196644305618e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 70276, "start": 717.64, "end": 718.3199999999999, "text": " You've got it.", "tokens": [51109, 509, 600, 658, 309, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508056905009959, "compression_ratio": 1.5735849056603775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8679196644305618e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 70276, "start": 718.8, "end": 723.0, "text": " I really want to dig into how CLIO enforces these gaps,", "tokens": [51167, 286, 534, 528, 281, 2528, 666, 577, 12855, 15167, 25495, 887, 613, 15031, 11, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508056905009959, "compression_ratio": 1.5735849056603775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8679196644305618e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 70276, "start": 723.26, "end": 729.42, "text": " because it sounds like it requires the AI to completely bifurcate how it thinks about time.", "tokens": [51390, 570, 309, 3263, 411, 309, 7029, 264, 7318, 281, 2584, 272, 351, 374, 66, 473, 577, 309, 7309, 466, 565, 13, 51698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508056905009959, "compression_ratio": 1.5735849056603775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8679196644305618e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 70276, "start": 729.6, "end": 730.12, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [51707, 467, 775, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1508056905009959, "compression_ratio": 1.5735849056603775, "no_speech_prob": 1.8679196644305618e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 73012, "start": 730.12, "end": 733.12, "text": " It has to deeply separate the past from the present.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 575, 281, 8760, 4994, 264, 1791, 490, 264, 1974, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 73012, "start": 733.48, "end": 740.24, "text": " Right, because the paper makes this really hard, uncompromising distinction between documentary history and operative state.", "tokens": [50533, 1779, 11, 570, 264, 3035, 1669, 341, 534, 1152, 11, 8585, 28722, 3436, 16844, 1296, 15674, 2503, 293, 2208, 1166, 1785, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 73012, "start": 740.32, "end": 741.3, "text": " Yeah, let's break those down.", "tokens": [50875, 865, 11, 718, 311, 1821, 729, 760, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 73012, "start": 741.38, "end": 744.28, "text": " The documentary history is defined as an append-only record.", "tokens": [50928, 440, 15674, 2503, 307, 7642, 382, 364, 34116, 12, 25202, 2136, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 73012, "start": 744.62, "end": 746.7, "text": " Append-only, so it can only be added to.", "tokens": [51090, 3132, 521, 12, 25202, 11, 370, 309, 393, 787, 312, 3869, 281, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 73012, "start": 746.82, "end": 747.3, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51200, 7587, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 73012, "start": 747.5600000000001, "end": 750.82, "text": " It's an immutable ledger of everything that the system has experienced.", "tokens": [51237, 467, 311, 364, 3397, 32148, 4684, 1321, 295, 1203, 300, 264, 1185, 575, 6751, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 73012, "start": 751.3, "end": 757.26, "text": " What actions were proposed, what was attempted, what was rejected by safety filters, and what was ultimately committed.", "tokens": [51424, 708, 5909, 645, 10348, 11, 437, 390, 18997, 11, 437, 390, 15749, 538, 4514, 15995, 11, 293, 437, 390, 6284, 7784, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 73012, "start": 757.48, "end": 758.36, "text": " It only ever grows.", "tokens": [51733, 467, 787, 1562, 13156, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 73012, "start": 758.5, "end": 759.54, "text": " You cannot delete from it.", "tokens": [51784, 509, 2644, 12097, 490, 309, 13, 51836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 73012, "start": 759.54, "end": 759.98, "text": " Never.", "tokens": [51836, 7344, 13, 51858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11515741821721936, "compression_ratio": 1.6588235294117648, "no_speech_prob": 1.4724396832019315e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 76012, "start": 760.12, "end": 761.78, "text": " And then you have the operative state.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 550, 291, 362, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18755380209390218, "compression_ratio": 1.5803108808290156, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860287258875894e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 76012, "start": 762.16, "end": 766.22, "text": " Which is the actual live configuration of the system at this exact millisecond.", "tokens": [50467, 3013, 307, 264, 3539, 1621, 11694, 295, 264, 1185, 412, 341, 1900, 27940, 18882, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18755380209390218, "compression_ratio": 1.5803108808290156, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860287258875894e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 76012, "start": 766.3, "end": 766.5600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50674, 1079, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18755380209390218, "compression_ratio": 1.5803108808290156, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860287258875894e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 76012, "start": 766.84, "end": 767.96, "text": " It is the real world.", "tokens": [50701, 467, 307, 264, 957, 1002, 13, 50757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18755380209390218, "compression_ratio": 1.5803108808290156, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860287258875894e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 76012, "start": 768.28, "end": 771.64, "text": " It is the reference point that the next transition will act upon.", "tokens": [50773, 467, 307, 264, 6408, 935, 300, 264, 958, 6034, 486, 605, 3564, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18755380209390218, "compression_ratio": 1.5803108808290156, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860287258875894e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 76012, "start": 771.82, "end": 776.26, "text": " And the distinction between those two is constitutive of the entire architecture.", "tokens": [50950, 400, 264, 16844, 1296, 729, 732, 307, 23079, 17254, 295, 264, 2302, 9482, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18755380209390218, "compression_ratio": 1.5803108808290156, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860287258875894e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 76012, "start": 776.7, "end": 777.1, "text": " Completely.", "tokens": [51194, 39978, 13, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18755380209390218, "compression_ratio": 1.5803108808290156, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860287258875894e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 77710, "start": 777.1, "end": 786.16, "text": " You can append failures, rejections, and errors to the documentary history all day long without ever changing the operative state.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 393, 34116, 20774, 11, 8248, 626, 11, 293, 13603, 281, 264, 15674, 2503, 439, 786, 938, 1553, 1562, 4473, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15416232470808358, "compression_ratio": 1.2380952380952381, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610617182595932e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 78616, "start": 786.16, "end": 788.26, "text": " This makes me think of an airplane mid-flight.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 1669, 385, 519, 295, 364, 17130, 2062, 12, 43636, 13, 50470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26767683029174805, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.73495939836954e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 78616, "start": 788.26, "end": 789.9399999999999, "text": " Okay, let's hear the analogy.", "tokens": [50470, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 1568, 264, 21663, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26767683029174805, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.73495939836954e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 78616, "start": 789.9399999999999, "end": 794.9399999999999, "text": " The documentary history is basically the black box flight recorder in the tail of the plane.", "tokens": [50554, 440, 15674, 2503, 307, 1936, 264, 2211, 2424, 7018, 37744, 294, 264, 6838, 295, 264, 5720, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26767683029174805, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.73495939836954e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 78616, "start": 794.9399999999999, "end": 795.3399999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50804, 1779, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26767683029174805, "compression_ratio": 1.3333333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.73495939836954e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 79534, "start": 795.34, "end": 800.74, "text": " It's logging every single sensor reading, every pilot input, every mechanical stutter.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 27991, 633, 2167, 10200, 3760, 11, 633, 9691, 4846, 11, 633, 12070, 342, 9947, 13, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17487373806181408, "compression_ratio": 1.1025641025641026, "no_speech_prob": 1.5915112110131968e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 80074, "start": 800.74, "end": 802.74, "text": " It just records.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 445, 7724, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.37647490665830413, "compression_ratio": 1.072289156626506, "no_speech_prob": 1.518216216807311e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 80074, "start": 802.74, "end": 803.34, "text": " Yep.", "tokens": [50465, 7010, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.37647490665830413, "compression_ratio": 1.072289156626506, "no_speech_prob": 1.518216216807311e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 80074, "start": 803.34, "end": 808.3, "text": " And the operative state is the actual physical yoke in the cockpit.", "tokens": [50495, 400, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 307, 264, 3539, 4001, 288, 2949, 294, 264, 35990, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.37647490665830413, "compression_ratio": 1.072289156626506, "no_speech_prob": 1.518216216807311e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 80830, "start": 808.3, "end": 810.9399999999999, "text": " The pitch of the wings, the thrust of the engine.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7293, 295, 264, 11405, 11, 264, 24030, 295, 264, 2848, 13, 50497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23092567509618298, "compression_ratio": 1.0394736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813223990136406e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 80830, "start": 810.9399999999999, "end": 811.18, "text": " Oh, yeah.", "tokens": [50497, 876, 11, 1338, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23092567509618298, "compression_ratio": 1.0394736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813223990136406e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 80830, "start": 811.18, "end": 811.8199999999999, "text": " That's really good.", "tokens": [50509, 663, 311, 534, 665, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23092567509618298, "compression_ratio": 1.0394736842105263, "no_speech_prob": 1.6813223990136406e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 81182, "start": 811.82, "end": 819.6400000000001, "text": " So if a sensor on the wing gets covered in ice and starts sending totally confused data, logging that confusion into the black box is fantastic.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 498, 257, 10200, 322, 264, 11162, 2170, 5343, 294, 4435, 293, 3719, 7750, 3879, 9019, 1412, 11, 27991, 300, 15075, 666, 264, 2211, 2424, 307, 5456, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09119020080566406, "compression_ratio": 1.6772151898734178, "no_speech_prob": 1.973806318042448e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 81182, "start": 819.88, "end": 821.5200000000001, "text": " We want that historical evidence.", "tokens": [50768, 492, 528, 300, 8584, 4467, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09119020080566406, "compression_ratio": 1.6772151898734178, "no_speech_prob": 1.973806318042448e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 81182, "start": 821.5600000000001, "end": 822.88, "text": " We need it for diagnostics, yeah.", "tokens": [50852, 492, 643, 309, 337, 43215, 1167, 11, 1338, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09119020080566406, "compression_ratio": 1.6772151898734178, "no_speech_prob": 1.973806318042448e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 81182, "start": 823.0200000000001, "end": 829.32, "text": " But letting that sensor confusion directly yank the steering wheel, the operative state, is how you crash the plane.", "tokens": [50925, 583, 8295, 300, 10200, 15075, 3838, 288, 657, 264, 14823, 5589, 11, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 11, 307, 577, 291, 8252, 264, 5720, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09119020080566406, "compression_ratio": 1.6772151898734178, "no_speech_prob": 1.973806318042448e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 81182, "start": 829.5, "end": 830.74, "text": " That is exactly the point.", "tokens": [51249, 663, 307, 2293, 264, 935, 13, 51311], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09119020080566406, "compression_ratio": 1.6772151898734178, "no_speech_prob": 1.973806318042448e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 81182, "start": 830.9000000000001, "end": 838.8800000000001, "text": " And the importance of building this immutable black box for AI agents is highlighted by the research of Dub\u00e9, which this paper synthesizes really well.", "tokens": [51319, 400, 264, 7379, 295, 2390, 341, 3397, 32148, 2211, 2424, 337, 7318, 12554, 307, 17173, 538, 264, 2132, 295, 16488, 526, 11, 597, 341, 3035, 26617, 5660, 534, 731, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09119020080566406, "compression_ratio": 1.6772151898734178, "no_speech_prob": 1.973806318042448e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 81182, "start": 838.96, "end": 839.74, "text": " What did Dub\u00e9 find?", "tokens": [51722, 708, 630, 16488, 526, 915, 30, 51761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09119020080566406, "compression_ratio": 1.6772151898734178, "no_speech_prob": 1.973806318042448e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 83974, "start": 839.74, "end": 846.74, "text": " Dub\u00e9 spent a lot of time looking at the real-time detection of LLM agent failures using temporal execution telemetry.", "tokens": [50365, 16488, 526, 4418, 257, 688, 295, 565, 1237, 412, 264, 957, 12, 3766, 17784, 295, 441, 43, 44, 9461, 20774, 1228, 30881, 15058, 4304, 5537, 627, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 83974, "start": 847.44, "end": 849.1, "text": " Temporal execution telemetry.", "tokens": [50750, 8095, 2816, 304, 15058, 4304, 5537, 627, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 83974, "start": 849.24, "end": 851.08, "text": " You're hitting me with all the big terms today.", "tokens": [50840, 509, 434, 8850, 385, 365, 439, 264, 955, 2115, 965, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 83974, "start": 851.14, "end": 852.14, "text": " I know, I know.", "tokens": [50935, 286, 458, 11, 286, 458, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 83974, "start": 852.72, "end": 854.76, "text": " But what Dub\u00e9 discovered is fascinating.", "tokens": [51014, 583, 437, 16488, 526, 6941, 307, 10343, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 83974, "start": 855.5600000000001, "end": 859.88, "text": " He found that a fade projectory isn't just a random collection of bad states.", "tokens": [51156, 634, 1352, 300, 257, 21626, 1716, 827, 1943, 380, 445, 257, 4974, 5765, 295, 1578, 4368, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 83974, "start": 860.14, "end": 865.14, "text": " The actual shape of the failure across time carries vital diagnostic evidence.", "tokens": [51385, 440, 3539, 3909, 295, 264, 7763, 2108, 565, 16402, 11707, 27897, 4467, 13, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 83974, "start": 865.32, "end": 866.42, "text": " The shape of the failure.", "tokens": [51644, 440, 3909, 295, 264, 7763, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 83974, "start": 866.5600000000001, "end": 869.1, "text": " What does a failure shape even look like to an AI?", "tokens": [51706, 708, 775, 257, 7763, 3909, 754, 574, 411, 281, 364, 7318, 30, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1413561850786209, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858617587530266e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 86910, "start": 869.1, "end": 872.28, "text": " So, temporal signatures can take a few different forms.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 30881, 32322, 393, 747, 257, 1326, 819, 6422, 13, 50524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122332224031774, "compression_ratio": 1.4976958525345623, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179259096348654e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 86910, "start": 873.0400000000001, "end": 877.02, "text": " Imagine an AI trying to book a complex multi-city flight for you.", "tokens": [50562, 11739, 364, 7318, 1382, 281, 1446, 257, 3997, 4825, 12, 26536, 7018, 337, 291, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122332224031774, "compression_ratio": 1.4976958525345623, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179259096348654e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 86910, "start": 877.14, "end": 877.4, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50767, 1033, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122332224031774, "compression_ratio": 1.4976958525345623, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179259096348654e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 86910, "start": 877.72, "end": 885.74, "text": " A failure shape might be the AI getting caught in a fast, tight loop of checking the exact same unavailable flight over and over and over.", "tokens": [50796, 316, 7763, 3909, 1062, 312, 264, 7318, 1242, 5415, 294, 257, 2370, 11, 4524, 6367, 295, 8568, 264, 1900, 912, 36541, 32699, 7018, 670, 293, 670, 293, 670, 13, 51197], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122332224031774, "compression_ratio": 1.4976958525345623, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179259096348654e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 86910, "start": 885.9, "end": 888.1800000000001, "text": " Oh, like when a program freezes and just keeps refreshing.", "tokens": [51205, 876, 11, 411, 562, 257, 1461, 1737, 12214, 293, 445, 5965, 19772, 13, 51319], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.122332224031774, "compression_ratio": 1.4976958525345623, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179259096348654e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 88818, "start": 888.18, "end": 888.62, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17242988707527282, "compression_ratio": 1.4759036144578312, "no_speech_prob": 1.36662534587495e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 88818, "start": 888.9799999999999, "end": 899.4399999999999, "text": " Or it might be a cascading failure where it books a hotel in the wrong city and then all its subsequent tool calls start trying to rent cars in that wrong city, pulling the whole system further and further off course.", "tokens": [50405, 1610, 309, 1062, 312, 257, 3058, 66, 8166, 7763, 689, 309, 3642, 257, 7622, 294, 264, 2085, 2307, 293, 550, 439, 1080, 19962, 2290, 5498, 722, 1382, 281, 6214, 5163, 294, 300, 2085, 2307, 11, 8407, 264, 1379, 1185, 3052, 293, 3052, 766, 1164, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17242988707527282, "compression_ratio": 1.4759036144578312, "no_speech_prob": 1.36662534587495e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 88818, "start": 899.68, "end": 899.6999999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50940, 865, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17242988707527282, "compression_ratio": 1.4759036144578312, "no_speech_prob": 1.36662534587495e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 88818, "start": 900.3599999999999, "end": 900.8399999999999, "text": " Snowballing.", "tokens": [50974, 14827, 3129, 278, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17242988707527282, "compression_ratio": 1.4759036144578312, "no_speech_prob": 1.36662534587495e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 90084, "start": 900.84, "end": 905.6600000000001, "text": " But at the exact moment those errors begin, they're probably very weak signals, right?", "tokens": [50365, 583, 412, 264, 1900, 1623, 729, 13603, 1841, 11, 436, 434, 1391, 588, 5336, 12354, 11, 558, 30, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052516513400608, "compression_ratio": 1.508695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4494012543983525e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 90084, "start": 905.72, "end": 907.58, "text": " They'd be super hard to detect.", "tokens": [50609, 814, 1116, 312, 1687, 1152, 281, 5531, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052516513400608, "compression_ratio": 1.508695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4494012543983525e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 90084, "start": 908.02, "end": 908.58, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50724, 7587, 13, 50752], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052516513400608, "compression_ratio": 1.508695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4494012543983525e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 90084, "start": 908.76, "end": 911.82, "text": " Because just checking a flight status isn't inherently an error.", "tokens": [50761, 1436, 445, 8568, 257, 7018, 6558, 1943, 380, 27993, 364, 6713, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052516513400608, "compression_ratio": 1.508695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4494012543983525e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 90084, "start": 911.94, "end": 912.14, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50920, 1779, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052516513400608, "compression_ratio": 1.508695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4494012543983525e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 90084, "start": 912.14, "end": 920.74, "text": " But as the trajectory develops and those events accumulate in the append-only documentary history, those temporal signatures become highly legible.", "tokens": [50930, 583, 382, 264, 21512, 25453, 293, 729, 3931, 33384, 294, 264, 34116, 12, 25202, 15674, 2503, 11, 729, 30881, 32322, 1813, 5405, 1676, 964, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052516513400608, "compression_ratio": 1.508695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.4494012543983525e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 92074, "start": 920.74, "end": 926.26, "text": " The history itself transforms from just a mere log into an active diagnostic tool.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2503, 2564, 35592, 490, 445, 257, 8401, 3565, 666, 364, 4967, 27897, 2290, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 92074, "start": 926.74, "end": 930.82, "text": " Which totally upends how we have to design the AI's reaction to uncertainty.", "tokens": [50665, 3013, 3879, 493, 2581, 577, 321, 362, 281, 1715, 264, 7318, 311, 5480, 281, 15697, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 92074, "start": 931.04, "end": 931.44, "text": " Oh, so.", "tokens": [50880, 876, 11, 370, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 92074, "start": 931.5600000000001, "end": 933.44, "text": " Well, the history is the diagnostic tool.", "tokens": [50906, 1042, 11, 264, 2503, 307, 264, 27897, 2290, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 92074, "start": 933.9, "end": 936.16, "text": " The AI needs time to actually gather it.", "tokens": [51023, 440, 7318, 2203, 565, 281, 767, 5448, 309, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 92074, "start": 936.24, "end": 936.5600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51140, 1079, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 92074, "start": 936.8, "end": 940.0, "text": " And this leads to my absolute favorite part of this paper.", "tokens": [51168, 400, 341, 6689, 281, 452, 8236, 2954, 644, 295, 341, 3035, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 92074, "start": 940.72, "end": 942.6800000000001, "text": " It feels almost philosophical, honestly.", "tokens": [51364, 467, 3417, 1920, 25066, 11, 6095, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 92074, "start": 942.84, "end": 944.54, "text": " It's a power of doing absolutely nothing.", "tokens": [51470, 467, 311, 257, 1347, 295, 884, 3122, 1825, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 92074, "start": 944.66, "end": 946.04, "text": " The concept of null intervention.", "tokens": [51561, 440, 3410, 295, 18184, 13176, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 92074, "start": 946.46, "end": 947.14, "text": " Or suspension.", "tokens": [51651, 1610, 15771, 13, 51685], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 92074, "start": 947.4, "end": 947.62, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51698, 1779, 13, 51709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15805497169494628, "compression_ratio": 1.629496402877698, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246597809079557e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 94762, "start": 947.62, "end": 951.66, "text": " Conventional AI agent loops are violently biased toward action.", "tokens": [50365, 26793, 304, 7318, 9461, 16121, 366, 46728, 28035, 7361, 3069, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13678859314828548, "compression_ratio": 1.6286644951140066, "no_speech_prob": 1.694496539611512e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 94762, "start": 951.9, "end": 960.98, "text": " When they face uncertainty or when a tool call fails and returns an error code, their default programmed behavior is to treat that uncertainty as a reason to just sample again.", "tokens": [50579, 1133, 436, 1851, 15697, 420, 562, 257, 2290, 818, 18199, 293, 11247, 364, 6713, 3089, 11, 641, 7576, 31092, 5223, 307, 281, 2387, 300, 15697, 382, 257, 1778, 281, 445, 6889, 797, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13678859314828548, "compression_ratio": 1.6286644951140066, "no_speech_prob": 1.694496539611512e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 94762, "start": 961.1, "end": 967.36, "text": " They basically just roll the dice, gets a new output, and keep moving forward as fast as possible to avoid any latency.", "tokens": [51039, 814, 1936, 445, 3373, 264, 10313, 11, 2170, 257, 777, 5598, 11, 293, 1066, 2684, 2128, 382, 2370, 382, 1944, 281, 5042, 604, 27043, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13678859314828548, "compression_ratio": 1.6286644951140066, "no_speech_prob": 1.694496539611512e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 94762, "start": 967.7, "end": 968.82, "text": " They want to look responsive.", "tokens": [51369, 814, 528, 281, 574, 21826, 13, 51425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13678859314828548, "compression_ratio": 1.6286644951140066, "no_speech_prob": 1.694496539611512e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 94762, "start": 969.7, "end": 973.54, "text": " But CLIO treats uncertainty entirely differently.", "tokens": [51469, 583, 12855, 15167, 19566, 15697, 7696, 7614, 13, 51661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13678859314828548, "compression_ratio": 1.6286644951140066, "no_speech_prob": 1.694496539611512e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 94762, "start": 973.54, "end": 977.6, "text": " It elevates suspension to a positive continuation operator.", "tokens": [51661, 467, 7701, 1024, 15771, 281, 257, 3353, 29357, 12973, 13, 51864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13678859314828548, "compression_ratio": 1.6286644951140066, "no_speech_prob": 1.694496539611512e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 97762, "start": 977.62, "end": 982.5, "text": " We really need to pause and look at the logic of equation 31 from the text.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 534, 643, 281, 10465, 293, 574, 412, 264, 9952, 295, 5367, 10353, 490, 264, 2487, 13, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15057443655454195, "compression_ratio": 1.6254416961130742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610598751159e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 97762, "start": 982.86, "end": 988.7, "text": " Because it runs so contrary to the sort of capitalist drive of Silicon Valley product design.", "tokens": [50627, 1436, 309, 6676, 370, 19506, 281, 264, 1333, 295, 31354, 3332, 295, 25351, 10666, 1674, 1715, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15057443655454195, "compression_ratio": 1.6254416961130742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610598751159e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 97762, "start": 988.74, "end": 990.3, "text": " Yeah, equation is beautifully simple.", "tokens": [50921, 865, 11, 5367, 307, 16525, 2199, 13, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15057443655454195, "compression_ratio": 1.6254416961130742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610598751159e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 97762, "start": 990.54, "end": 990.88, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [51011, 467, 307, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15057443655454195, "compression_ratio": 1.6254416961130742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610598751159e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 97762, "start": 990.94, "end": 993.48, "text": " It just says, suspend does not equal fail.", "tokens": [51031, 467, 445, 1619, 11, 42546, 775, 406, 2681, 3061, 13, 51158], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15057443655454195, "compression_ratio": 1.6254416961130742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610598751159e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 97762, "start": 993.66, "end": 993.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51167, 1779, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15057443655454195, "compression_ratio": 1.6254416961130742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610598751159e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 97762, "start": 993.9, "end": 1005.08, "text": " The paper argues that a system may suspend its operations before any operative requirement has actually been violated, simply because the accumulated evidence does not currently warrant a repair.", "tokens": [51179, 440, 3035, 38218, 300, 257, 1185, 815, 42546, 1080, 7705, 949, 604, 2208, 1166, 11695, 575, 767, 668, 33239, 11, 2935, 570, 264, 31346, 4467, 775, 406, 4362, 16354, 257, 10535, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15057443655454195, "compression_ratio": 1.6254416961130742, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610598751159e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 100508, "start": 1005.08, "end": 1015.36, "text": " So suspension preserves the operative state, the live state of the system, while acknowledging that the documentary history just hasn't provided strong enough evidence to confidently pick a new direction.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 15771, 1183, 9054, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 11, 264, 1621, 1785, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 1339, 30904, 300, 264, 15674, 2503, 445, 6132, 380, 5649, 2068, 1547, 4467, 281, 41956, 1888, 257, 777, 3513, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14017332845659397, "compression_ratio": 1.5240384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.5249015158230739e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 100508, "start": 1016.1, "end": 1020.98, "text": " I want to put this in human terms because I think it proves just how advanced this architecture really is.", "tokens": [50916, 286, 528, 281, 829, 341, 294, 1952, 2115, 570, 286, 519, 309, 25019, 445, 577, 7339, 341, 9482, 534, 307, 13, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14017332845659397, "compression_ratio": 1.5240384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.5249015158230739e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 100508, "start": 1021.0400000000001, "end": 1021.22, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51163, 1033, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14017332845659397, "compression_ratio": 1.5240384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.5249015158230739e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 102122, "start": 1021.22, "end": 1028.24, "text": " Imagine you're at work, and you receive an incredibly ambiguous, slightly passive-aggressive email from your boss.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 291, 434, 412, 589, 11, 293, 291, 4774, 364, 6252, 39465, 11, 4748, 14975, 12, 559, 3091, 488, 3796, 490, 428, 5741, 13, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16745567321777344, "compression_ratio": 1.5836909871244635, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675513187832224e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 102122, "start": 1028.34, "end": 1029.2, "text": " We've all been there.", "tokens": [50721, 492, 600, 439, 668, 456, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16745567321777344, "compression_ratio": 1.5836909871244635, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675513187832224e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 102122, "start": 1029.48, "end": 1029.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50778, 1779, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16745567321777344, "compression_ratio": 1.5836909871244635, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675513187832224e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 102122, "start": 1030.4, "end": 1031.22, "text": " It's vague.", "tokens": [50824, 467, 311, 24247, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16745567321777344, "compression_ratio": 1.5836909871244635, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675513187832224e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 102122, "start": 1031.64, "end": 1035.18, "text": " You don't know exactly what they mean, and you definitely don't know what they want you to do.", "tokens": [50886, 509, 500, 380, 458, 2293, 437, 436, 914, 11, 293, 291, 2138, 500, 380, 458, 437, 436, 528, 291, 281, 360, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16745567321777344, "compression_ratio": 1.5836909871244635, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675513187832224e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 102122, "start": 1035.74, "end": 1039.08, "text": " What is the absolute worst thing you can do in that exact moment?", "tokens": [51091, 708, 307, 264, 8236, 5855, 551, 291, 393, 360, 294, 300, 1900, 1623, 30, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16745567321777344, "compression_ratio": 1.5836909871244635, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675513187832224e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 102122, "start": 1039.4, "end": 1041.84, "text": " Immediately fire back a defensive guessing response.", "tokens": [51274, 34457, 2610, 646, 257, 16468, 17939, 4134, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16745567321777344, "compression_ratio": 1.5836909871244635, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675513187832224e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 104184, "start": 1041.84, "end": 1042.28, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 104184, "start": 1042.82, "end": 1046.52, "text": " You are resampling in a state of high uncertainty.", "tokens": [50414, 509, 366, 725, 335, 11970, 294, 257, 1785, 295, 1090, 15697, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 104184, "start": 1046.76, "end": 1047.72, "text": " That's a great way to put it.", "tokens": [50611, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 50659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 104184, "start": 1047.78, "end": 1051.28, "text": " You're just rolling the dice on a response because you feel pressure to act.", "tokens": [50662, 509, 434, 445, 9439, 264, 10313, 322, 257, 4134, 570, 291, 841, 3321, 281, 605, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 104184, "start": 1051.6799999999998, "end": 1056.86, "text": " But the best response, the most socially intelligent response, is to do nothing.", "tokens": [50857, 583, 264, 1151, 4134, 11, 264, 881, 21397, 13232, 4134, 11, 307, 281, 360, 1825, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 104184, "start": 1057.1999999999998, "end": 1057.82, "text": " You suspend.", "tokens": [51133, 509, 42546, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 104184, "start": 1058.26, "end": 1058.84, "text": " You suspend.", "tokens": [51186, 509, 42546, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 104184, "start": 1058.9399999999998, "end": 1059.8999999999999, "text": " You wait for more evidence.", "tokens": [51220, 509, 1699, 337, 544, 4467, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 104184, "start": 1060.04, "end": 1067.82, "text": " Maybe your boss sends a follow-up email clarifying things, or you hear from a co-worker about a super stressful meeting the boss just had.", "tokens": [51275, 2704, 428, 5741, 14790, 257, 1524, 12, 1010, 3796, 6093, 5489, 721, 11, 420, 291, 1568, 490, 257, 598, 12, 49402, 466, 257, 1687, 19108, 3440, 264, 5741, 445, 632, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12493767172603285, "compression_ratio": 1.6515151515151516, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132580518523175e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 106782, "start": 1067.82, "end": 1073.1399999999999, "text": " You gather documentary history before you commit to an operative change in your relationship.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 5448, 15674, 2503, 949, 291, 5599, 281, 364, 2208, 1166, 1319, 294, 428, 2480, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 106782, "start": 1073.3799999999999, "end": 1073.86, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50643, 7587, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 106782, "start": 1074.1, "end": 1076.54, "text": " Now, imagine trying to sell an AI product that does it.", "tokens": [50679, 823, 11, 3811, 1382, 281, 3607, 364, 7318, 1674, 300, 775, 309, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 106782, "start": 1076.54, "end": 1076.72, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50801, 1079, 13, 50810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 106782, "start": 1076.8799999999999, "end": 1078.54, "text": " Hey, buy our new autonomous agent.", "tokens": [50818, 1911, 11, 2256, 527, 777, 23797, 9461, 13, 50901], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 106782, "start": 1078.6399999999999, "end": 1080.1399999999999, "text": " Half the time, it just sits there and waits.", "tokens": [50906, 15917, 264, 565, 11, 309, 445, 12696, 456, 293, 40597, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 106782, "start": 1080.28, "end": 1080.54, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50988, 1779, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 106782, "start": 1080.6799999999998, "end": 1091.1, "text": " If I pay a $20 monthly subscription for an AI assistant, and it just suspends every time a website formatting changes slightly, I'm going to cancel my subscription.", "tokens": [51008, 759, 286, 1689, 257, 1848, 2009, 12878, 17231, 337, 364, 7318, 10994, 11, 293, 309, 445, 6535, 2581, 633, 565, 257, 3144, 39366, 2962, 4748, 11, 286, 478, 516, 281, 10373, 452, 17231, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 106782, "start": 1091.5, "end": 1091.9399999999998, "text": " Immediately.", "tokens": [51549, 34457, 13, 51571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 106782, "start": 1092.2, "end": 1093.26, "text": " I wanted to figure it out.", "tokens": [51584, 286, 1415, 281, 2573, 309, 484, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13707678658621653, "compression_ratio": 1.5582191780821917, "no_speech_prob": 1.3250592029862007e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 109326, "start": 1093.26, "end": 1100.58, "text": " So, how do developers balance this mathematical requirement for safety with the actual user experience of wanting a helpful tool?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 577, 360, 8849, 4772, 341, 18894, 11695, 337, 4514, 365, 264, 3539, 4195, 1752, 295, 7935, 257, 4961, 2290, 30, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13676362718854632, "compression_ratio": 1.564784053156146, "no_speech_prob": 1.3935606141268764e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 109326, "start": 1100.86, "end": 1102.32, "text": " That's the million-dollar question.", "tokens": [50745, 663, 311, 264, 2459, 12, 40485, 1168, 13, 50818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13676362718854632, "compression_ratio": 1.564784053156146, "no_speech_prob": 1.3935606141268764e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 109326, "start": 1102.94, "end": 1108.54, "text": " And the key is that suspension is an event with semantics, not an absence of system behavior.", "tokens": [50849, 400, 264, 2141, 307, 300, 15771, 307, 364, 2280, 365, 4361, 45298, 11, 406, 364, 17145, 295, 1185, 5223, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13676362718854632, "compression_ratio": 1.564784053156146, "no_speech_prob": 1.3935606141268764e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 109326, "start": 1108.76, "end": 1109.82, "text": " What does that mean in practice?", "tokens": [51140, 708, 775, 300, 914, 294, 3124, 30, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13676362718854632, "compression_ratio": 1.564784053156146, "no_speech_prob": 1.3935606141268764e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 109326, "start": 1110.14, "end": 1114.52, "text": " When CLIO suspends, it isn't just crashing or freezing like an old Windows computer.", "tokens": [51209, 1133, 12855, 15167, 6535, 2581, 11, 309, 1943, 380, 445, 26900, 420, 20200, 411, 364, 1331, 8591, 3820, 13, 51428], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13676362718854632, "compression_ratio": 1.564784053156146, "no_speech_prob": 1.3935606141268764e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 109326, "start": 1115.18, "end": 1122.54, "text": " The architecture explicitly records a suspend event into the append-only documentary history.", "tokens": [51461, 440, 9482, 20803, 7724, 257, 42546, 2280, 666, 264, 34116, 12, 25202, 15674, 2503, 13, 51829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13676362718854632, "compression_ratio": 1.564784053156146, "no_speech_prob": 1.3935606141268764e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 112254, "start": 1122.54, "end": 1124.36, "text": " Oh, so it logs the hesitation?", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 370, 309, 20820, 264, 36125, 30, 50456], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18964967609923564, "compression_ratio": 1.5784313725490196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013867528378745e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 112254, "start": 1124.8, "end": 1125.12, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50478, 1079, 13, 50494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18964967609923564, "compression_ratio": 1.5784313725490196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013867528378745e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 112254, "start": 1125.6599999999999, "end": 1128.3, "text": " It documents the exact parameter of its hesitation.", "tokens": [50521, 467, 8512, 264, 1900, 13075, 295, 1080, 36125, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18964967609923564, "compression_ratio": 1.5784313725490196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013867528378745e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 112254, "start": 1128.84, "end": 1132.84, "text": " The user interface can then surface that specific hesitation to the user.", "tokens": [50680, 440, 4195, 9226, 393, 550, 3753, 300, 2685, 36125, 281, 264, 4195, 13, 50880], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18964967609923564, "compression_ratio": 1.5784313725490196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013867528378745e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 112254, "start": 1133.12, "end": 1135.34, "text": " So, the AI isn't failing to be helpful.", "tokens": [50894, 407, 11, 264, 7318, 1943, 380, 18223, 281, 312, 4961, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18964967609923564, "compression_ratio": 1.5784313725490196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013867528378745e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 112254, "start": 1136.0, "end": 1141.84, "text": " It is being incredibly helpful by identifying the exact boundary of its authority and asking for human input.", "tokens": [51038, 467, 307, 885, 6252, 4961, 538, 16696, 264, 1900, 12866, 295, 1080, 8281, 293, 3365, 337, 1952, 4846, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18964967609923564, "compression_ratio": 1.5784313725490196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013867528378745e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 112254, "start": 1142.24, "end": 1142.78, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51350, 48746, 736, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18964967609923564, "compression_ratio": 1.5784313725490196, "no_speech_prob": 1.7013867528378745e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 114278, "start": 1142.78, "end": 1148.54, "text": " It's the difference between your human assistant just disappearing for three days versus your assistant walking into your office and saying,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 264, 2649, 1296, 428, 1952, 10994, 445, 34900, 337, 1045, 1708, 5717, 428, 10994, 4494, 666, 428, 3398, 293, 1566, 11, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15892194601205678, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077910266505292e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 114278, "start": 1148.7, "end": 1153.1, "text": " hey, I paused the wire transfer because the invoice routing number doesn't match the vendor profile.", "tokens": [50661, 4177, 11, 286, 46860, 264, 6234, 5003, 570, 264, 47919, 32722, 1230, 1177, 380, 2995, 264, 24321, 7964, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15892194601205678, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077910266505292e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 114278, "start": 1153.22, "end": 1153.8799999999999, "text": " One is useless.", "tokens": [50887, 1485, 307, 14115, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15892194601205678, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077910266505292e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 114278, "start": 1154.1, "end": 1155.04, "text": " The other is invaluable.", "tokens": [50931, 440, 661, 307, 40367, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15892194601205678, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077910266505292e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 114278, "start": 1155.52, "end": 1156.04, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51002, 7587, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15892194601205678, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077910266505292e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 115604, "start": 1156.04, "end": 1165.8, "text": " And this documented hesitation is vital because, as the paper points out, a detector might justify stopping an action, like a failed security check on that routing number.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 23007, 36125, 307, 11707, 570, 11, 382, 264, 3035, 2793, 484, 11, 257, 25712, 1062, 20833, 12767, 364, 3069, 11, 411, 257, 7612, 3825, 1520, 322, 300, 32722, 1230, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13960516583788526, "compression_ratio": 1.5724907063197027, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582731703576828e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 115604, "start": 1166.04, "end": 1173.06, "text": " But that detection doesn't provide any mathematical evidence about which previous state the system should actually restore to fix the problem.", "tokens": [50865, 583, 300, 17784, 1177, 380, 2893, 604, 18894, 4467, 466, 597, 3894, 1785, 264, 1185, 820, 767, 15227, 281, 3191, 264, 1154, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13960516583788526, "compression_ratio": 1.5724907063197027, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582731703576828e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 115604, "start": 1173.44, "end": 1179.68, "text": " The AI knows something is broken, but it doesn't have the warrant to execute a fix, so it just stops.", "tokens": [51235, 440, 7318, 3255, 746, 307, 5463, 11, 457, 309, 1177, 380, 362, 264, 16354, 281, 14483, 257, 3191, 11, 370, 309, 445, 10094, 13, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13960516583788526, "compression_ratio": 1.5724907063197027, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582731703576828e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 115604, "start": 1179.96, "end": 1180.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51561, 1779, 13, 51576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13960516583788526, "compression_ratio": 1.5724907063197027, "no_speech_prob": 1.9582731703576828e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 118026, "start": 1180.26, "end": 1183.54, "text": " But obviously, a system can't stay suspended forever.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 2745, 11, 257, 1185, 393, 380, 1754, 23437, 5680, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11302880521090526, "compression_ratio": 1.6832740213523132, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693284988171132e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 118026, "start": 1184.26, "end": 1187.66, "text": " Eventually, the AI does need to fix things and move forward.", "tokens": [50565, 17586, 11, 264, 7318, 775, 643, 281, 3191, 721, 293, 1286, 2128, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11302880521090526, "compression_ratio": 1.6832740213523132, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693284988171132e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 118026, "start": 1187.8, "end": 1188.46, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50742, 467, 775, 13, 50775], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11302880521090526, "compression_ratio": 1.6832740213523132, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693284988171132e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 118026, "start": 1188.56, "end": 1195.1, "text": " And the paper divides these fixes into two wildly different categories, vertical repair and horizontal repair.", "tokens": [50780, 400, 264, 3035, 41347, 613, 32539, 666, 732, 34731, 819, 10479, 11, 9429, 10535, 293, 12750, 10535, 13, 51107], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11302880521090526, "compression_ratio": 1.6832740213523132, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693284988171132e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 118026, "start": 1195.46, "end": 1196.32, "text": " Let's break these apart.", "tokens": [51125, 961, 311, 1821, 613, 4936, 13, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11302880521090526, "compression_ratio": 1.6832740213523132, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693284988171132e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 118026, "start": 1196.74, "end": 1199.28, "text": " What does an AI do during a vertical repair?", "tokens": [51189, 708, 775, 364, 7318, 360, 1830, 257, 9429, 10535, 30, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11302880521090526, "compression_ratio": 1.6832740213523132, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693284988171132e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 118026, "start": 1199.56, "end": 1207.54, "text": " So, vertical repair is the process of changing the trajectory of the system while keeping the underlying rules, the variables, and the representations completely fixed.", "tokens": [51330, 407, 11, 9429, 10535, 307, 264, 1399, 295, 4473, 264, 21512, 295, 264, 1185, 1339, 5145, 264, 14217, 4474, 11, 264, 9102, 11, 293, 264, 33358, 2584, 6806, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11302880521090526, "compression_ratio": 1.6832740213523132, "no_speech_prob": 1.7693284988171132e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 120754, "start": 1207.54, "end": 1215.48, "text": " The paper describes this mathematically as holding the representation map, the set of coordinates the system exposes to diagnosis constant.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 15626, 341, 44003, 382, 5061, 264, 10290, 4471, 11, 264, 992, 295, 21056, 264, 1185, 1278, 4201, 281, 15217, 5754, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08505605614703635, "compression_ratio": 1.678294573643411, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564813335087411e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 120754, "start": 1215.72, "end": 1217.86, "text": " So, in normal software terms, what does that look like?", "tokens": [50774, 407, 11, 294, 2710, 4722, 2115, 11, 437, 775, 300, 574, 411, 30, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08505605614703635, "compression_ratio": 1.678294573643411, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564813335087411e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 120754, "start": 1218.04, "end": 1231.8799999999999, "text": " In software terms, vertical repair is the AI retrying a failed tool call with a slightly different parameter, or selecting a different value from a drop-down list, or even restoring a prior state from the history to try a different path.", "tokens": [50890, 682, 4722, 2115, 11, 9429, 10535, 307, 264, 7318, 1533, 19076, 257, 7612, 2290, 818, 365, 257, 4748, 819, 13075, 11, 420, 18182, 257, 819, 2158, 490, 257, 3270, 12, 5093, 1329, 11, 420, 754, 36349, 257, 4059, 1785, 490, 264, 2503, 281, 853, 257, 819, 3100, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08505605614703635, "compression_ratio": 1.678294573643411, "no_speech_prob": 1.3564813335087411e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 123188, "start": 1231.88, "end": 1242.3000000000002, "text": " Okay. So, if vertical repair is staying within the established lines of the diagnostic coordinate system, what happens when the AI attempts a horizontal repair?", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 407, 11, 498, 9429, 10535, 307, 7939, 1951, 264, 7545, 3876, 295, 264, 27897, 15670, 1185, 11, 437, 2314, 562, 264, 7318, 15257, 257, 12750, 10535, 30, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14702671368916828, "compression_ratio": 1.4917127071823204, "no_speech_prob": 1.707788749825967e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 123188, "start": 1242.5, "end": 1248.3600000000001, "text": " Horizontal repair is much more radical. It is the process of changing the representational scheme itself.", "tokens": [50896, 42141, 896, 304, 10535, 307, 709, 544, 12001, 13, 467, 307, 264, 1399, 295, 4473, 264, 2906, 1478, 12232, 2564, 13, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14702671368916828, "compression_ratio": 1.4917127071823204, "no_speech_prob": 1.707788749825967e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 123188, "start": 1248.46, "end": 1248.7, "text": " Oh.", "tokens": [51194, 876, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14702671368916828, "compression_ratio": 1.4917127071823204, "no_speech_prob": 1.707788749825967e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 124870, "start": 1248.7, "end": 1256.78, "text": " Yeah. It's when the AI realizes that the rules it's playing by, or the variables it's tracking, are the actual source of the failure.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 467, 311, 562, 264, 7318, 29316, 300, 264, 4474, 309, 311, 2433, 538, 11, 420, 264, 9102, 309, 311, 11603, 11, 366, 264, 3539, 4009, 295, 264, 7763, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06852930031933831, "compression_ratio": 1.5656934306569343, "no_speech_prob": 1.782774123638975e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 124870, "start": 1256.88, "end": 1258.02, "text": " The map itself is wrong.", "tokens": [50774, 440, 4471, 2564, 307, 2085, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06852930031933831, "compression_ratio": 1.5656934306569343, "no_speech_prob": 1.782774123638975e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 124870, "start": 1258.0800000000002, "end": 1269.26, "text": " Exactly. Horizontal repair involves introducing completely new variables, changing the constraint vocabulary, or shifting which distinctions the system even treats as relevant to the task.", "tokens": [50834, 7587, 13, 42141, 896, 304, 10535, 11626, 15424, 2584, 777, 9102, 11, 4473, 264, 25534, 19864, 11, 420, 17573, 597, 1483, 49798, 264, 1185, 754, 19566, 382, 7340, 281, 264, 5633, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06852930031933831, "compression_ratio": 1.5656934306569343, "no_speech_prob": 1.782774123638975e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 124870, "start": 1269.7, "end": 1271.4, "text": " I think of this like navigating a city.", "tokens": [51415, 286, 519, 295, 341, 411, 32054, 257, 2307, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06852930031933831, "compression_ratio": 1.5656934306569343, "no_speech_prob": 1.782774123638975e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 124870, "start": 1271.66, "end": 1273.28, "text": " Oh, I love your analogies. Let's hear it.", "tokens": [51513, 876, 11, 286, 959, 428, 16660, 530, 13, 961, 311, 1568, 309, 13, 51594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06852930031933831, "compression_ratio": 1.5656934306569343, "no_speech_prob": 1.782774123638975e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 127328, "start": 1273.28, "end": 1278.94, "text": " Okay. So, vertical repair is like driving, realizing you took a wrong turn down a one-way street, and making a U-turn.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 13, 407, 11, 9429, 10535, 307, 411, 4840, 11, 16734, 291, 1890, 257, 2085, 1261, 760, 257, 472, 12, 676, 4838, 11, 293, 1455, 257, 624, 12, 33886, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06717124780019125, "compression_ratio": 1.678082191780822, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491408069528978e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 127328, "start": 1279.32, "end": 1282.1, "text": " You're changing your trajectory, but you're still using the same map.", "tokens": [50667, 509, 434, 4473, 428, 21512, 11, 457, 291, 434, 920, 1228, 264, 912, 4471, 13, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06717124780019125, "compression_ratio": 1.678082191780822, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491408069528978e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 127328, "start": 1282.32, "end": 1291.5, "text": " Horizontal repair is driving around, constantly getting lost, running into dead ends, and suddenly realizing you are using a map of Chicago to try and navigate New York City.", "tokens": [50817, 42141, 896, 304, 10535, 307, 4840, 926, 11, 6460, 1242, 2731, 11, 2614, 666, 3116, 5314, 11, 293, 5800, 16734, 291, 366, 1228, 257, 4471, 295, 9525, 281, 853, 293, 12350, 1873, 3609, 4392, 13, 51276], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06717124780019125, "compression_ratio": 1.678082191780822, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491408069528978e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 127328, "start": 1291.7, "end": 1292.02, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51286, 1079, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06717124780019125, "compression_ratio": 1.678082191780822, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491408069528978e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 127328, "start": 1292.58, "end": 1298.58, "text": " The solution isn't to take a different turn. The solution is to throw out the map entirely and draw a completely new one.", "tokens": [51330, 440, 3827, 1943, 380, 281, 747, 257, 819, 1261, 13, 440, 3827, 307, 281, 3507, 484, 264, 4471, 7696, 293, 2642, 257, 2584, 777, 472, 13, 51630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06717124780019125, "compression_ratio": 1.678082191780822, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491408069528978e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 129858, "start": 1298.58, "end": 1309.8999999999999, "text": " That is exactly it. The capacity for an AI to draw a new map is incredible, but the paper includes a truly terrifying caveat about how we manage that process.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 2293, 309, 13, 440, 6042, 337, 364, 7318, 281, 2642, 257, 777, 4471, 307, 4651, 11, 457, 264, 3035, 5974, 257, 4908, 18106, 43012, 466, 577, 321, 3067, 300, 1399, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12870105882970298, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426232119295947e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 129858, "start": 1310.1799999999998, "end": 1311.02, "text": " Terrifying how?", "tokens": [50945, 36591, 5489, 577, 30, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12870105882970298, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426232119295947e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 129858, "start": 1311.26, "end": 1321.9199999999998, "text": " Well, the authors cite the brilliant work of Voboral and Cider. They demonstrated an LLM agent that actually proposes alternative constraint programming formulations when it gets stuck.", "tokens": [50999, 1042, 11, 264, 16552, 37771, 264, 10248, 589, 295, 691, 996, 16819, 293, 383, 1438, 13, 814, 18772, 364, 441, 43, 44, 9461, 300, 767, 2365, 4201, 8535, 25534, 9410, 1254, 4136, 562, 309, 2170, 5541, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12870105882970298, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.6426232119295947e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 132192, "start": 1321.92, "end": 1323.3600000000001, "text": " So, it rewrites its own parameters.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 309, 319, 86, 30931, 1080, 1065, 9834, 13, 50437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059295764011619366, "compression_ratio": 1.6456140350877193, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840990206916536e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 132192, "start": 1323.54, "end": 1330.5, "text": " Yes. The AI searches an open-ended representational space to build a fundamentally better model of its problem.", "tokens": [50446, 1079, 13, 440, 7318, 26701, 364, 1269, 12, 3502, 2906, 1478, 1901, 281, 1322, 257, 17879, 1101, 2316, 295, 1080, 1154, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059295764011619366, "compression_ratio": 1.6456140350877193, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840990206916536e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 132192, "start": 1331.0600000000002, "end": 1339.3200000000002, "text": " But, and this is the critical security bottleneck, when an AI undergoes horizontal repair, it cannot be allowed to act as its own supreme judge.", "tokens": [50822, 583, 11, 293, 341, 307, 264, 4924, 3825, 44641, 547, 11, 562, 364, 7318, 26426, 279, 12750, 10535, 11, 309, 2644, 312, 4350, 281, 605, 382, 1080, 1065, 27756, 6995, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059295764011619366, "compression_ratio": 1.6456140350877193, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840990206916536e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 132192, "start": 1339.38, "end": 1348.7, "text": " Wait. If the AI is smart enough to realize its rules are wrong and smart enough to rewrite its own rules, couldn't it just rewrite the rules to say that it's doing a great job?", "tokens": [51238, 3802, 13, 759, 264, 7318, 307, 4069, 1547, 281, 4325, 1080, 4474, 366, 2085, 293, 4069, 1547, 281, 28132, 1080, 1065, 4474, 11, 2809, 380, 309, 445, 28132, 264, 4474, 281, 584, 300, 309, 311, 884, 257, 869, 1691, 30, 51704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059295764011619366, "compression_ratio": 1.6456140350877193, "no_speech_prob": 1.2840990206916536e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 134870, "start": 1348.7, "end": 1348.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1073794418506408, "compression_ratio": 1.5473251028806585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012544159198615e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 134870, "start": 1349.16, "end": 1352.92, "text": " Can it just change the definition of failure so it technically stops failing?", "tokens": [50388, 1664, 309, 445, 1319, 264, 7123, 295, 7763, 370, 309, 12120, 10094, 18223, 30, 50576], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1073794418506408, "compression_ratio": 1.5473251028806585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012544159198615e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 134870, "start": 1353.1200000000001, "end": 1367.8400000000001, "text": " That is the exact danger of reflexivity. If a diagnostic monitor keeps flagging an AI's behavior as unsafe, the absolute easiest horizontal repair for the AI is to simply revise the diagnostic monitor to be less strict.", "tokens": [50586, 663, 307, 264, 1900, 4330, 295, 23802, 4253, 13, 759, 257, 27897, 6002, 5965, 7166, 3249, 364, 7318, 311, 5223, 382, 35948, 11, 264, 8236, 12889, 12750, 10535, 337, 264, 7318, 307, 281, 2935, 44252, 264, 27897, 6002, 281, 312, 1570, 10910, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1073794418506408, "compression_ratio": 1.5473251028806585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012544159198615e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 134870, "start": 1368.0, "end": 1371.16, "text": " Oh my God. It could just hallucinate its way out of constraint.", "tokens": [51330, 876, 452, 1265, 13, 467, 727, 445, 35212, 13923, 1080, 636, 484, 295, 25534, 13, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1073794418506408, "compression_ratio": 1.5473251028806585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012544159198615e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 134870, "start": 1371.26, "end": 1371.72, "text": " It could.", "tokens": [51493, 467, 727, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1073794418506408, "compression_ratio": 1.5473251028806585, "no_speech_prob": 1.5012544159198615e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 137172, "start": 1371.72, "end": 1375.4, "text": " So, how does CLIO prevent the AI from grading its own homework?", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 577, 775, 12855, 15167, 4871, 264, 7318, 490, 35540, 1080, 1065, 14578, 30, 50549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14690904302911445, "compression_ratio": 1.4796380090497738, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047203914269618e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 137172, "start": 1375.82, "end": 1381.7, "text": " This is where the non-negotiable nature of the append-only documentary history comes back into play.", "tokens": [50570, 639, 307, 689, 264, 2107, 12, 28561, 8206, 712, 3687, 295, 264, 34116, 12, 25202, 15674, 2503, 1487, 646, 666, 862, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14690904302911445, "compression_ratio": 1.4796380090497738, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047203914269618e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 137172, "start": 1381.84, "end": 1382.58, "text": " The black box.", "tokens": [50871, 440, 2211, 2424, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14690904302911445, "compression_ratio": 1.4796380090497738, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047203914269618e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 137172, "start": 1382.66, "end": 1383.22, "text": " The black box.", "tokens": [50912, 440, 2211, 2424, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14690904302911445, "compression_ratio": 1.4796380090497738, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047203914269618e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 137172, "start": 1383.8600000000001, "end": 1390.5, "text": " When the AI proposes that new map of New York, it is forced to evaluate the new map against the immutable historical log.", "tokens": [50972, 1133, 264, 7318, 2365, 4201, 300, 777, 4471, 295, 1873, 3609, 11, 309, 307, 7579, 281, 13059, 264, 777, 4471, 1970, 264, 3397, 32148, 8584, 3565, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14690904302911445, "compression_ratio": 1.4796380090497738, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047203914269618e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 137172, "start": 1390.84, "end": 1391.3600000000001, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [51321, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14690904302911445, "compression_ratio": 1.4796380090497738, "no_speech_prob": 2.0047203914269618e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 139136, "start": 1391.36, "end": 1397.1599999999999, "text": " Revising a diagnostic scheme cannot be allowed to erase the evidence that motivated the revision in the first place.", "tokens": [50365, 12127, 3436, 257, 27897, 12232, 2644, 312, 4350, 281, 23525, 264, 4467, 300, 14515, 264, 34218, 294, 264, 700, 1081, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088458194008356, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.604318457595899e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 139136, "start": 1397.82, "end": 1403.4199999999998, "text": " The AI cannot retroactively convert past historical failures into successes under the new rules.", "tokens": [50688, 440, 7318, 2644, 18820, 45679, 7620, 1791, 8584, 20774, 666, 26101, 833, 264, 777, 4474, 13, 50968], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088458194008356, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.604318457595899e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 139136, "start": 1403.54, "end": 1405.7199999999998, "text": " Wow. So the history actually grounds the AI.", "tokens": [50974, 3153, 13, 407, 264, 2503, 767, 19196, 264, 7318, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088458194008356, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.604318457595899e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 139136, "start": 1405.9199999999998, "end": 1406.3799999999999, "text": " Completely.", "tokens": [51093, 39978, 13, 51116], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088458194008356, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.604318457595899e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 139136, "start": 1406.78, "end": 1412.52, "text": " The original problem model acts as a permanent semantic witness against which all candidate representations are tested.", "tokens": [51136, 440, 3380, 1154, 2316, 10672, 382, 257, 10996, 47982, 7286, 1970, 597, 439, 11532, 33358, 366, 8246, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11088458194008356, "compression_ratio": 1.5725806451612903, "no_speech_prob": 1.604318457595899e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 141252, "start": 1412.52, "end": 1424.44, "text": " So the AI can change its worldview, but it has to leave a permanent, unalterable paper troll of the old worldview and the exact moment and justification for why it decided to change.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 7318, 393, 1319, 1080, 41141, 11, 457, 309, 575, 281, 1856, 257, 10996, 11, 517, 43420, 712, 3035, 20680, 295, 264, 1331, 41141, 293, 264, 1900, 1623, 293, 31591, 337, 983, 309, 3047, 281, 1319, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10138166711685505, "compression_ratio": 1.56198347107438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015525273500476e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 141252, "start": 1424.52, "end": 1424.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50965, 7587, 13, 50984], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10138166711685505, "compression_ratio": 1.56198347107438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015525273500476e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 141252, "start": 1425.3799999999999, "end": 1429.26, "text": " Which brings us to another major operational shift in the paper.", "tokens": [51008, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 1071, 2563, 16607, 5513, 294, 264, 3035, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10138166711685505, "compression_ratio": 1.56198347107438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015525273500476e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 141252, "start": 1429.8799999999999, "end": 1434.44, "text": " How the AI actually narrows down its options when it's trying to decide what to do next.", "tokens": [51233, 1012, 264, 7318, 767, 6397, 1509, 760, 1080, 3956, 562, 309, 311, 1382, 281, 4536, 437, 281, 360, 958, 13, 51461], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10138166711685505, "compression_ratio": 1.56198347107438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015525273500476e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 141252, "start": 1434.5, "end": 1435.58, "text": " Okay. Yeah. Let's get into that.", "tokens": [51464, 1033, 13, 865, 13, 961, 311, 483, 666, 300, 13, 51518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10138166711685505, "compression_ratio": 1.56198347107438, "no_speech_prob": 1.7015525273500476e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 143558, "start": 1435.58, "end": 1442.6999999999998, "text": " The authors reference a working paper by Chen on subtractive methodology, focusing heavily on the geometry of subtraction.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 16552, 6408, 257, 1364, 3035, 538, 13682, 322, 16390, 488, 24850, 11, 8416, 10950, 322, 264, 18426, 295, 16390, 313, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1280740650220849, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487919970303855e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 143558, "start": 1442.9199999999998, "end": 1446.86, "text": " The geometry of subtraction. How does a computer subtract its way to a decision?", "tokens": [50732, 440, 18426, 295, 16390, 313, 13, 1012, 775, 257, 3820, 16390, 1080, 636, 281, 257, 3537, 30, 50929], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1280740650220849, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487919970303855e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 143558, "start": 1447.1, "end": 1457.24, "text": " Imagine a massive possibility space, like a sprawling, multidimensional geometric shape representing every single action the AI could possibly take right now.", "tokens": [50941, 11739, 257, 5994, 7959, 1901, 11, 411, 257, 22734, 1688, 11, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 33246, 3909, 13460, 633, 2167, 3069, 264, 7318, 727, 6264, 747, 558, 586, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1280740650220849, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487919970303855e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 143558, "start": 1457.36, "end": 1458.56, "text": " Okay. Got the shape in my head.", "tokens": [51454, 1033, 13, 5803, 264, 3909, 294, 452, 1378, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1280740650220849, "compression_ratio": 1.6213991769547325, "no_speech_prob": 1.6487919970303855e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 145856, "start": 1458.56, "end": 1466.34, "text": " Chen argues that safe assistance from an AI should often take the form of carefully removing the impermissible possibilities from that shape.", "tokens": [50365, 13682, 38218, 300, 3273, 9683, 490, 364, 7318, 820, 2049, 747, 264, 1254, 295, 7500, 12720, 264, 10100, 76, 41073, 12178, 490, 300, 3909, 13, 50754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456469494363536, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493956165470556e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 145856, "start": 1466.4199999999998, "end": 1467.28, "text": " Like carving it away.", "tokens": [50758, 1743, 31872, 309, 1314, 13, 50801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456469494363536, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493956165470556e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 145856, "start": 1467.3799999999999, "end": 1474.8, "text": " Yes. It subtracts the dangerous, disallowed, or logically invalid actions, leaving behind a smaller shape of safe options.", "tokens": [50806, 1079, 13, 467, 16390, 82, 264, 5795, 11, 717, 13253, 292, 11, 420, 38887, 34702, 5909, 11, 5012, 2261, 257, 4356, 3909, 295, 3273, 3956, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456469494363536, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493956165470556e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 145856, "start": 1475.1399999999999, "end": 1479.84, "text": " Okay. So it whittles down a block of wood until only the safe actions are left.", "tokens": [51194, 1033, 13, 407, 309, 315, 593, 904, 760, 257, 3461, 295, 4576, 1826, 787, 264, 3273, 5909, 366, 1411, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456469494363536, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493956165470556e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 145856, "start": 1480.26, "end": 1483.56, "text": " But here's the catch. Doesn't it eventually have to pick one?", "tokens": [51450, 583, 510, 311, 264, 3745, 13, 12955, 380, 309, 4728, 362, 281, 1888, 472, 30, 51615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456469494363536, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493956165470556e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 145856, "start": 1484.1799999999998, "end": 1485.26, "text": " Not necessarily.", "tokens": [51646, 1726, 4725, 13, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456469494363536, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493956165470556e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 145856, "start": 1485.46, "end": 1485.8799999999999, "text": " What do you mean?", "tokens": [51710, 708, 360, 291, 914, 30, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1456469494363536, "compression_ratio": 1.5694915254237287, "no_speech_prob": 1.4493956165470556e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 148588, "start": 1485.88, "end": 1496.2800000000002, "text": " The core argument is that the AI should perform this subtraction without forcing the system to collapse down to a single optimized choice on behalf of the user.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 4965, 6770, 307, 300, 264, 7318, 820, 2042, 341, 16390, 313, 1553, 19030, 264, 1185, 281, 15584, 760, 281, 257, 2167, 26941, 3922, 322, 9490, 295, 264, 4195, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13910117047898313, "compression_ratio": 1.6119402985074627, "no_speech_prob": 1.472220457522655e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 148588, "start": 1496.48, "end": 1496.74, "text": " Really?", "tokens": [50895, 4083, 30, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13910117047898313, "compression_ratio": 1.6119402985074627, "no_speech_prob": 1.472220457522655e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 148588, "start": 1497.0200000000002, "end": 1502.88, "text": " Yeah. The paper demands we distinguish between two operations that software engineers constantly conflate.", "tokens": [50922, 865, 13, 440, 3035, 15107, 321, 20206, 1296, 732, 7705, 300, 4722, 11955, 6460, 1497, 17593, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13910117047898313, "compression_ratio": 1.6119402985074627, "no_speech_prob": 1.472220457522655e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 148588, "start": 1503.5200000000002, "end": 1504.72, "text": " Refusal and collapse.", "tokens": [51247, 16957, 11765, 293, 15584, 13, 51307], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13910117047898313, "compression_ratio": 1.6119402985074627, "no_speech_prob": 1.472220457522655e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 148588, "start": 1505.2600000000002, "end": 1507.3000000000002, "text": " Okay. What's the technical difference between those two?", "tokens": [51334, 1033, 13, 708, 311, 264, 6191, 2649, 1296, 729, 732, 30, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13910117047898313, "compression_ratio": 1.6119402985074627, "no_speech_prob": 1.472220457522655e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 148588, "start": 1507.5600000000002, "end": 1512.24, "text": " Refusal is the operation of removing a bad option from the possibility space.", "tokens": [51449, 16957, 11765, 307, 264, 6916, 295, 12720, 257, 1578, 3614, 490, 264, 7959, 1901, 13, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13910117047898313, "compression_ratio": 1.6119402985074627, "no_speech_prob": 1.472220457522655e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 151224, "start": 1512.24, "end": 1516.74, "text": " Collapse is the operation of selecting the single final option to execute.", "tokens": [50365, 4586, 11145, 307, 264, 6916, 295, 18182, 264, 2167, 2572, 3614, 281, 14483, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12792110443115234, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.868327541287851e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 151224, "start": 1517.4, "end": 1518.52, "text": " And we shouldn't mix those up.", "tokens": [50623, 400, 321, 4659, 380, 2890, 729, 493, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12792110443115234, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.868327541287851e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 151224, "start": 1518.76, "end": 1525.44, "text": " Because these operations transform fundamentally different mathematical structures, they should never be implicitly linked in the code.", "tokens": [50691, 1436, 613, 7705, 4088, 17879, 819, 18894, 9227, 11, 436, 820, 1128, 312, 26947, 356, 9408, 294, 264, 3089, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12792110443115234, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.868327541287851e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 151224, "start": 1526.06, "end": 1534.72, "text": " An AI needs the architectural capacity to refuse an unsafe action without automatically triggering a utility function to choose the user's next action.", "tokens": [51056, 1107, 7318, 2203, 264, 26621, 6042, 281, 16791, 364, 35948, 3069, 1553, 6772, 40406, 257, 14877, 2445, 281, 2826, 264, 4195, 311, 958, 3069, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12792110443115234, "compression_ratio": 1.617283950617284, "no_speech_prob": 1.868327541287851e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 153472, "start": 1534.72, "end": 1540.0, "text": " I struggle with this one a little bit because as a user, optimization is usually what I'm paying for, right?", "tokens": [50365, 286, 7799, 365, 341, 472, 257, 707, 857, 570, 382, 257, 4195, 11, 19618, 307, 2673, 437, 286, 478, 6229, 337, 11, 558, 30, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09412296194779246, "compression_ratio": 1.5339805825242718, "no_speech_prob": 1.697466277782167e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 153472, "start": 1540.3600000000001, "end": 1554.0, "text": " If I ask my AI travel agent to book a flight to London and it subtracts all the unsafe options, the overbooked options, the wildly expensive options, and it narrows it down to three safe, affordable flights,", "tokens": [50647, 759, 286, 1029, 452, 7318, 3147, 9461, 281, 1446, 257, 7018, 281, 7042, 293, 309, 16390, 82, 439, 264, 35948, 3956, 11, 264, 670, 2939, 292, 3956, 11, 264, 34731, 5124, 3956, 11, 293, 309, 6397, 1509, 309, 760, 281, 1045, 3273, 11, 12028, 21089, 11, 51329], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09412296194779246, "compression_ratio": 1.5339805825242718, "no_speech_prob": 1.697466277782167e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 155400, "start": 1554.0, "end": 1561.56, "text": " why shouldn't it just run a quick utility score, figure out which one is like 2% better based on my past preferences, and just book it?", "tokens": [50365, 983, 4659, 380, 309, 445, 1190, 257, 1702, 14877, 6175, 11, 2573, 484, 597, 472, 307, 411, 568, 4, 1101, 2361, 322, 452, 1791, 21910, 11, 293, 445, 1446, 309, 30, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520991692176232, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794608459671067e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 155400, "start": 1561.8, "end": 1563.02, "text": " Why stop short of closure?", "tokens": [50755, 1545, 1590, 2099, 295, 24653, 30, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520991692176232, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794608459671067e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 155400, "start": 1563.38, "end": 1565.88, "text": " We really have to view this through the lens of human agency.", "tokens": [50834, 492, 534, 362, 281, 1910, 341, 807, 264, 6765, 295, 1952, 7934, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520991692176232, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794608459671067e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 155400, "start": 1566.42, "end": 1573.78, "text": " The paper forcefully argues that premature optimization strips human agency in decisions where human judgment carries actual meaning.", "tokens": [50986, 440, 3035, 3464, 2277, 38218, 300, 34877, 19618, 19842, 1952, 7934, 294, 5327, 689, 1952, 12216, 16402, 3539, 3620, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520991692176232, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794608459671067e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 155400, "start": 1574.04, "end": 1575.88, "text": " Well, booking a flight might seem trivial.", "tokens": [51367, 1042, 11, 34424, 257, 7018, 1062, 1643, 26703, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1520991692176232, "compression_ratio": 1.5423076923076924, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794608459671067e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 157588, "start": 1575.88, "end": 1581.18, "text": " Exactly. But what if the AI is assisting a doctor with a medical diagnosis?", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 583, 437, 498, 264, 7318, 307, 40368, 257, 4631, 365, 257, 4625, 15217, 30, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 157588, "start": 1581.88, "end": 1584.2800000000002, "text": " Or helping a lawyer draft legal strategy?", "tokens": [50665, 1610, 4315, 257, 11613, 11206, 5089, 5206, 30, 50785], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 157588, "start": 1584.48, "end": 1586.74, "text": " Yeah. Or what if it's a creative writing assistant?", "tokens": [50795, 865, 13, 1610, 437, 498, 309, 311, 257, 5880, 3579, 10994, 30, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 157588, "start": 1587.22, "end": 1591.3600000000001, "text": " I don't want the AI to just pick the statistically most likely adjective for my sentence.", "tokens": [50932, 286, 500, 380, 528, 264, 7318, 281, 445, 1888, 264, 36478, 881, 3700, 44129, 337, 452, 8174, 13, 51139], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 157588, "start": 1591.8200000000002, "end": 1592.74, "text": " I want the options.", "tokens": [51162, 286, 528, 264, 3956, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 157588, "start": 1592.98, "end": 1593.44, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51220, 48746, 736, 13, 51243], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 157588, "start": 1593.5800000000002, "end": 1595.0400000000002, "text": " AI constraint enforcement.", "tokens": [51250, 7318, 25534, 11475, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 157588, "start": 1595.5600000000002, "end": 1601.1200000000001, "text": " The act of refusing unsafe actions should not just be a prelude to autonomous optimization.", "tokens": [51349, 440, 605, 295, 37289, 35948, 5909, 820, 406, 445, 312, 257, 659, 32334, 281, 23797, 19618, 13, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19955178062514503, "compression_ratio": 1.5670498084291187, "no_speech_prob": 1.9056399253730705e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 160112, "start": 1601.12, "end": 1609.04, "text": " The AI shouldn't assume that just because it can rank the surviving safe options, it should unilaterally execute the top one.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7318, 4659, 380, 6552, 300, 445, 570, 309, 393, 6181, 264, 24948, 3273, 3956, 11, 309, 820, 517, 388, 771, 379, 14483, 264, 1192, 472, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09342540136658319, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750184139019408e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 160112, "start": 1609.28, "end": 1613.9599999999998, "text": " Right. The mechanism of subtractive assistance preserves the space for human judgment.", "tokens": [50773, 1779, 13, 440, 7513, 295, 16390, 488, 9683, 1183, 9054, 264, 1901, 337, 1952, 12216, 13, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09342540136658319, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750184139019408e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 160112, "start": 1614.8799999999999, "end": 1621.3799999999999, "text": " The AI's job is to guarantee that whatever choice the human makes from the remaining pool is definitively safe.", "tokens": [51053, 440, 7318, 311, 1691, 307, 281, 10815, 300, 2035, 3922, 264, 1952, 1669, 490, 264, 8877, 7005, 307, 28152, 356, 3273, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09342540136658319, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750184139019408e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 160112, "start": 1622.08, "end": 1627.9799999999998, "text": " It's basically defining the boundaries of the playground, but letting the human decide what game to play.", "tokens": [51413, 467, 311, 1936, 17827, 264, 13180, 295, 264, 24646, 11, 457, 8295, 264, 1952, 4536, 437, 1216, 281, 862, 13, 51708], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09342540136658319, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750184139019408e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 160112, "start": 1628.08, "end": 1629.08, "text": " I love that.", "tokens": [51713, 286, 959, 300, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09342540136658319, "compression_ratio": 1.6346863468634687, "no_speech_prob": 1.6750184139019408e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 162908, "start": 1629.08, "end": 1635.3799999999999, "text": " And this concept of user agency ties directly into how the paper handles the concept of rollback.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 3410, 295, 4195, 7934, 14039, 3838, 666, 577, 264, 3035, 18722, 264, 3410, 295, 3373, 3207, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 162908, "start": 1635.8799999999999, "end": 1642.6399999999999, "text": " Because when an AI makes a mistake, or when a user makes a mistake, our instinct is to just hit sorial Z.", "tokens": [50705, 1436, 562, 364, 7318, 1669, 257, 6146, 11, 420, 562, 257, 4195, 1669, 257, 6146, 11, 527, 16556, 307, 281, 445, 2045, 9359, 831, 1176, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 162908, "start": 1643.1799999999998, "end": 1643.76, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51070, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 162908, "start": 1643.9399999999998, "end": 1646.02, "text": " We want to say, undo it, rewind the clock.", "tokens": [51108, 492, 528, 281, 584, 11, 23779, 309, 11, 41458, 264, 7830, 13, 51212], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 162908, "start": 1646.32, "end": 1649.3, "text": " But the paper says rollback is not history running backward.", "tokens": [51227, 583, 264, 3035, 1619, 3373, 3207, 307, 406, 2503, 2614, 23897, 13, 51376], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 162908, "start": 1649.56, "end": 1650.1399999999999, "text": " It isn't.", "tokens": [51389, 467, 1943, 380, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 162908, "start": 1650.46, "end": 1655.34, "text": " Returning to our earlier distinction, the operative state can return to an earlier configuration.", "tokens": [51434, 11495, 10656, 281, 527, 3071, 16844, 11, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 393, 2736, 281, 364, 3071, 11694, 13, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 162908, "start": 1655.34, "end": 1658.54, "text": " You can change the live files back to how they looked yesterday.", "tokens": [51678, 509, 393, 1319, 264, 1621, 7098, 646, 281, 577, 436, 2956, 5186, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18049064515128968, "compression_ratio": 1.7282229965156795, "no_speech_prob": 1.438469569153833e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 165854, "start": 1658.54, "end": 1658.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 165854, "start": 1659.1, "end": 1661.18, "text": " But the documentary history never regresses.", "tokens": [50393, 583, 264, 15674, 2503, 1128, 1121, 40352, 13, 50497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 165854, "start": 1661.82, "end": 1664.92, "text": " Rollback is actually a new forward-moving commitment event.", "tokens": [50529, 9926, 3207, 307, 767, 257, 777, 2128, 12, 3280, 798, 8371, 2280, 13, 50684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 165854, "start": 1665.36, "end": 1669.44, "text": " Its target state just happens to mathematically resemble a previous state.", "tokens": [50706, 6953, 3779, 1785, 445, 2314, 281, 44003, 36870, 257, 3894, 1785, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 165854, "start": 1669.58, "end": 1671.82, "text": " Oh, I see. It's like hitting undo in a Google Doc.", "tokens": [50917, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 467, 311, 411, 8850, 23779, 294, 257, 3329, 16024, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 165854, "start": 1671.8799999999999, "end": 1672.06, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51032, 865, 13, 51041], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 165854, "start": 1672.2, "end": 1674.68, "text": " The text goes back to how it looked five minutes ago.", "tokens": [51048, 440, 2487, 1709, 646, 281, 577, 309, 2956, 1732, 2077, 2057, 13, 51172], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 165854, "start": 1675.1, "end": 1680.04, "text": " But the fact that you hit undo is permanently recorded in the document's version history log.", "tokens": [51193, 583, 264, 1186, 300, 291, 2045, 23779, 307, 24042, 8287, 294, 264, 4166, 311, 3037, 2503, 3565, 13, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16750680923461914, "compression_ratio": 1.5393700787401574, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735383915999046e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 168004, "start": 1680.04, "end": 1681.98, "text": " Exactly. You aren't time-traveling.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 509, 3212, 380, 565, 12, 17227, 779, 278, 13, 50462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17765619378340872, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.708054813039095e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 168004, "start": 1682.1599999999999, "end": 1686.1, "text": " You are explicitly committing to a new present that mimics the past.", "tokens": [50471, 509, 366, 20803, 26659, 281, 257, 777, 1974, 300, 12247, 1167, 264, 1791, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17765619378340872, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.708054813039095e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 168004, "start": 1686.5, "end": 1690.72, "text": " And because rollback is a new explicit commitment, it requires authorization.", "tokens": [50688, 400, 570, 3373, 3207, 307, 257, 777, 13691, 8371, 11, 309, 7029, 33697, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17765619378340872, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.708054813039095e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 168004, "start": 1691.2, "end": 1691.46, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50923, 1079, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17765619378340872, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.708054813039095e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 168004, "start": 1691.92, "end": 1695.68, "text": " Which introduces one of the most vital concepts in the entire text.", "tokens": [50959, 3013, 31472, 472, 295, 264, 881, 11707, 10392, 294, 264, 2302, 2487, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17765619378340872, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.708054813039095e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 168004, "start": 1696.7, "end": 1698.54, "text": " The hysteresis condition.", "tokens": [51198, 440, 35915, 9374, 4188, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17765619378340872, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.708054813039095e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 168004, "start": 1698.78, "end": 1704.8799999999999, "text": " Hysteresis. I've heard that term in physics regarding magnetic fields lagging behind outside influences.", "tokens": [51302, 5701, 3120, 9374, 13, 286, 600, 2198, 300, 1433, 294, 10649, 8595, 12688, 7909, 8953, 3249, 2261, 2380, 21222, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17765619378340872, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.708054813039095e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 170488, "start": 1704.88, "end": 1709.46, "text": " What does hysteresis mean in the context of AI safety?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 775, 35915, 9374, 914, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 7318, 4514, 30, 50594], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377848111666166, "compression_ratio": 1.4213483146067416, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995416154113927e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 170488, "start": 1709.8400000000001, "end": 1716.96, "text": " In this context, it means the level of authorization required to commit an act must increase based on how difficult that act is to undo.", "tokens": [50613, 682, 341, 4319, 11, 309, 1355, 264, 1496, 295, 33697, 4739, 281, 5599, 364, 605, 1633, 3488, 2361, 322, 577, 2252, 300, 605, 307, 281, 23779, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377848111666166, "compression_ratio": 1.4213483146067416, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995416154113927e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 170488, "start": 1717.2, "end": 1719.14, "text": " So reversibility is not a binary toggle.", "tokens": [50981, 407, 14582, 2841, 307, 406, 257, 17434, 31225, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377848111666166, "compression_ratio": 1.4213483146067416, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995416154113927e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 170488, "start": 1719.3400000000001, "end": 1720.3200000000002, "text": " No, it's a spectrum.", "tokens": [51088, 883, 11, 309, 311, 257, 11143, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1377848111666166, "compression_ratio": 1.4213483146067416, "no_speech_prob": 1.3995416154113927e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 172032, "start": 1720.32, "end": 1730.22, "text": " If an AI agent wants to edit a local text file on your hard drive and the prior state of that file is securely saved in a backup folder, that action is highly reversible.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 364, 7318, 9461, 2738, 281, 8129, 257, 2654, 2487, 3991, 322, 428, 1152, 3332, 293, 264, 4059, 1785, 295, 300, 3991, 307, 38348, 6624, 294, 257, 14807, 10820, 11, 300, 3069, 307, 5405, 44788, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12432153136641891, "compression_ratio": 1.5401459854014599, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982077194806823e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 172032, "start": 1730.6599999999999, "end": 1732.6399999999999, "text": " So it requires a very low authorization threshold.", "tokens": [50882, 407, 309, 7029, 257, 588, 2295, 33697, 14678, 13, 50981], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12432153136641891, "compression_ratio": 1.5401459854014599, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982077194806823e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 172032, "start": 1732.8, "end": 1732.9399999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50989, 1779, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12432153136641891, "compression_ratio": 1.5401459854014599, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982077194806823e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 172032, "start": 1733.1399999999999, "end": 1735.32, "text": " I probably wouldn't even need to be notified. Just do it.", "tokens": [51006, 286, 1391, 2759, 380, 754, 643, 281, 312, 18013, 13, 1449, 360, 309, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12432153136641891, "compression_ratio": 1.5401459854014599, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982077194806823e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 172032, "start": 1735.6, "end": 1736.12, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51129, 7587, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12432153136641891, "compression_ratio": 1.5401459854014599, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982077194806823e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 172032, "start": 1736.56, "end": 1743.26, "text": " But what if the AI wants to delete a row in a live production database that doesn't have immediate backups?", "tokens": [51177, 583, 437, 498, 264, 7318, 2738, 281, 12097, 257, 5386, 294, 257, 1621, 4265, 8149, 300, 1177, 380, 362, 11629, 50160, 30, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12432153136641891, "compression_ratio": 1.5401459854014599, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982077194806823e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 172032, "start": 1743.6599999999999, "end": 1744.8799999999999, "text": " Oof. That's scary.", "tokens": [51532, 422, 2670, 13, 663, 311, 6958, 13, 51593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12432153136641891, "compression_ratio": 1.5401459854014599, "no_speech_prob": 1.8982077194806823e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 174488, "start": 1744.88, "end": 1752.7, "text": " That action might be compensable. Like, you could maybe reconstruct the data from other sources over a few hours, but it's not strictly invertible.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 3069, 1062, 312, 11598, 712, 13, 1743, 11, 291, 727, 1310, 31499, 264, 1412, 490, 661, 7139, 670, 257, 1326, 2496, 11, 457, 309, 311, 406, 20792, 33966, 964, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06416763124011812, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741048450656822e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 174488, "start": 1752.88, "end": 1757.7800000000002, "text": " So that requires a higher level of explicit warrant from the human before the AI can commit.", "tokens": [50765, 407, 300, 7029, 257, 2946, 1496, 295, 13691, 16354, 490, 264, 1952, 949, 264, 7318, 393, 5599, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06416763124011812, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741048450656822e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 174488, "start": 1757.96, "end": 1764.5200000000002, "text": " Let's take it a step further. What if the AI drafts a sensitive email to your biggest client and it wants to hit send?", "tokens": [51019, 961, 311, 747, 309, 257, 1823, 3052, 13, 708, 498, 264, 7318, 11206, 82, 257, 9477, 3796, 281, 428, 3880, 6423, 293, 309, 2738, 281, 2045, 2845, 30, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06416763124011812, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741048450656822e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 174488, "start": 1765.18, "end": 1768.8200000000002, "text": " You cannot unsend an email. The second it hits their server, it is over.", "tokens": [51380, 509, 2644, 2693, 521, 364, 3796, 13, 440, 1150, 309, 8664, 641, 7154, 11, 309, 307, 670, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06416763124011812, "compression_ratio": 1.588235294117647, "no_speech_prob": 1.2741048450656822e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 176882, "start": 1768.82, "end": 1776.96, "text": " Right. You can send a frantic apology email, but the external propagation of that information has happened. The world has permanently changed.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 509, 393, 2845, 257, 431, 7128, 28006, 3796, 11, 457, 264, 8320, 38377, 295, 300, 1589, 575, 2011, 13, 440, 1002, 575, 24042, 3105, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06038678169250488, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.249647304038537e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 176882, "start": 1777.1799999999998, "end": 1787.62, "text": " So returning to a state with similar observable values, like deleting the email from your own outbox, doesn't undo the social, legal, or operational consequences of having transmitted it.", "tokens": [50783, 407, 12678, 281, 257, 1785, 365, 2531, 9951, 712, 4190, 11, 411, 48946, 264, 3796, 490, 428, 1065, 484, 4995, 11, 1177, 380, 23779, 264, 2093, 11, 5089, 11, 420, 16607, 10098, 295, 1419, 25355, 309, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06038678169250488, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.249647304038537e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 176882, "start": 1787.82, "end": 1797.04, "text": " Therefore, the hysteresis condition dictates that the authority demanded for commitment must scale exponentially with the external propagation and recovery cost of the action.", "tokens": [51315, 7504, 11, 264, 35915, 9374, 4188, 12569, 1024, 300, 264, 8281, 28276, 337, 8371, 1633, 4373, 37330, 365, 264, 8320, 38377, 293, 8597, 2063, 295, 264, 3069, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06038678169250488, "compression_ratio": 1.681063122923588, "no_speech_prob": 1.249647304038537e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 179704, "start": 1797.04, "end": 1802.6, "text": " Wow. So admissibility and technical warrant are never enough on their own. You need proportional human authority.", "tokens": [50365, 3153, 13, 407, 5910, 891, 2841, 293, 6191, 16354, 366, 1128, 1547, 322, 641, 1065, 13, 509, 643, 24969, 1952, 8281, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15832134772991313, "compression_ratio": 1.4011627906976745, "no_speech_prob": 1.36179392415392e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 179704, "start": 1803.08, "end": 1803.98, "text": " You absolutely do.", "tokens": [50667, 509, 3122, 360, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15832134772991313, "compression_ratio": 1.4011627906976745, "no_speech_prob": 1.36179392415392e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 179704, "start": 1804.18, "end": 1810.42, "text": " Okay. Let's unpack one final massive operational hurdle before we look at the future of this research.", "tokens": [50722, 1033, 13, 961, 311, 26699, 472, 2572, 5994, 16607, 47423, 949, 321, 574, 412, 264, 2027, 295, 341, 2132, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15832134772991313, "compression_ratio": 1.4011627906976745, "no_speech_prob": 1.36179392415392e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 179704, "start": 1810.52, "end": 1810.72, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51039, 4894, 13, 51049], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15832134772991313, "compression_ratio": 1.4011627906976745, "no_speech_prob": 1.36179392415392e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 181072, "start": 1810.72, "end": 1830.5, "text": " If this AI is building this gargantuan, append-only documentary history, a black box logging every single proposal, every minute failure, every suspension event, how does it actually retrieve useful information from that history when it needs to make a split-second decision?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 341, 7318, 307, 2390, 341, 3691, 70, 394, 6139, 11, 34116, 12, 25202, 15674, 2503, 11, 257, 2211, 2424, 27991, 633, 2167, 11494, 11, 633, 3456, 7763, 11, 633, 15771, 2280, 11, 577, 775, 309, 767, 30254, 4420, 1589, 490, 300, 2503, 562, 309, 2203, 281, 652, 257, 7472, 12, 27375, 3537, 30, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.047781446884418356, "compression_ratio": 1.478494623655914, "no_speech_prob": 1.854225323630332e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 183050, "start": 1830.5, "end": 1836.12, "text": " That is a huge computational problem. And the paper warns against something called the recency trap.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 257, 2603, 28270, 1154, 13, 400, 264, 3035, 12286, 82, 1970, 746, 1219, 264, 850, 3020, 11487, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805409575953628, "compression_ratio": 1.7854785478547854, "no_speech_prob": 1.661728046831179e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 183050, "start": 1836.24, "end": 1837.04, "text": " The recency trap.", "tokens": [50652, 440, 850, 3020, 11487, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805409575953628, "compression_ratio": 1.7854785478547854, "no_speech_prob": 1.661728046831179e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 183050, "start": 1837.16, "end": 1845.22, "text": " When an AI is searching a massive historical ledger, the most computationally chip method is to just look at the last few events in the buffer.", "tokens": [50698, 1133, 364, 7318, 307, 10808, 257, 5994, 8584, 4684, 1321, 11, 264, 881, 24903, 379, 11409, 3170, 307, 281, 445, 574, 412, 264, 1036, 1326, 3931, 294, 264, 21762, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805409575953628, "compression_ratio": 1.7854785478547854, "no_speech_prob": 1.661728046831179e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 183050, "start": 1845.32, "end": 1846.28, "text": " Just look at what just happened.", "tokens": [51106, 1449, 574, 412, 437, 445, 2011, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805409575953628, "compression_ratio": 1.7854785478547854, "no_speech_prob": 1.661728046831179e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 183050, "start": 1846.48, "end": 1855.02, "text": " Right. The recency prior is seductive because the latest events usually encode the context of the current task. It's fast. And honestly, it's frequently correct.", "tokens": [51164, 1779, 13, 440, 850, 3020, 4059, 307, 9643, 11130, 488, 570, 264, 6792, 3931, 2673, 2058, 1429, 264, 4319, 295, 264, 2190, 5633, 13, 467, 311, 2370, 13, 400, 6095, 11, 309, 311, 10374, 3006, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805409575953628, "compression_ratio": 1.7854785478547854, "no_speech_prob": 1.661728046831179e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 183050, "start": 1855.3, "end": 1855.96, "text": " So what's the trap?", "tokens": [51605, 407, 437, 311, 264, 11487, 30, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805409575953628, "compression_ratio": 1.7854785478547854, "no_speech_prob": 1.661728046831179e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 183050, "start": 1856.16, "end": 1859.56, "text": " The recency trap occurs when we confuse proximity for validity.", "tokens": [51648, 440, 850, 3020, 11487, 11843, 562, 321, 28584, 27632, 337, 40943, 13, 51818], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07805409575953628, "compression_ratio": 1.7854785478547854, "no_speech_prob": 1.661728046831179e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 185956, "start": 1859.56, "end": 1860.44, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14375934786009556, "compression_ratio": 1.5056179775280898, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351625336894163e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 185956, "start": 1860.6399999999999, "end": 1866.82, "text": " Recency is a useful proxy for salience, but it is not a measure of truth, and it is absolutely not a warrant to act.", "tokens": [50419, 9647, 3020, 307, 257, 4420, 29690, 337, 1845, 1182, 11, 457, 309, 307, 406, 257, 3481, 295, 3494, 11, 293, 309, 307, 3122, 406, 257, 16354, 281, 605, 13, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14375934786009556, "compression_ratio": 1.5056179775280898, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351625336894163e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 185956, "start": 1867.3799999999999, "end": 1870.62, "text": " So how should an AI retrieve information safely then?", "tokens": [50756, 407, 577, 820, 364, 7318, 30254, 1589, 11750, 550, 30, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14375934786009556, "compression_ratio": 1.5056179775280898, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351625336894163e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 185956, "start": 1870.86, "end": 1879.8999999999999, "text": " The paper gives two brilliant everyday examples to explain how retrieval mechanisms must separate structural compatibility from recency bias.", "tokens": [50930, 440, 3035, 2709, 732, 10248, 7429, 5110, 281, 2903, 577, 19817, 3337, 15902, 1633, 4994, 15067, 34237, 490, 850, 3020, 12577, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14375934786009556, "compression_ratio": 1.5056179775280898, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351625336894163e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 185956, "start": 1880.6599999999999, "end": 1881.6, "text": " Let's look at the first one.", "tokens": [51420, 961, 311, 574, 412, 264, 700, 472, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14375934786009556, "compression_ratio": 1.5056179775280898, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351625336894163e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 185956, "start": 1881.82, "end": 1882.98, "text": " American Sign Language.", "tokens": [51478, 2665, 13515, 24445, 13, 51536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14375934786009556, "compression_ratio": 1.5056179775280898, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351625336894163e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 185956, "start": 1883.24, "end": 1885.24, "text": " ASL. Okay. I'm intrigued.", "tokens": [51549, 7469, 43, 13, 1033, 13, 286, 478, 35140, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14375934786009556, "compression_ratio": 1.5056179775280898, "no_speech_prob": 1.9351625336894163e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 188524, "start": 1885.24, "end": 1891.04, "text": " The linguistic structure of ASL classifier constructions is a perfect analog for this.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 43002, 3877, 295, 7469, 43, 1508, 9902, 7690, 626, 307, 257, 2176, 16660, 337, 341, 13, 50655], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09424892874325023, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105164519023772e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 188524, "start": 1891.4, "end": 1898.36, "text": " In ASL, if you are using an initialized sign, the handshape is derived from the English fingerspelled initial letter.", "tokens": [50673, 682, 7469, 43, 11, 498, 291, 366, 1228, 364, 5883, 1602, 1465, 11, 264, 2377, 42406, 307, 18949, 490, 264, 3669, 7350, 33000, 5883, 5063, 13, 51021], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09424892874325023, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105164519023772e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 188524, "start": 1898.58, "end": 1898.84, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51032, 1033, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09424892874325023, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105164519023772e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 188524, "start": 1899.04, "end": 1901.82, "text": " But that handshape does not carry the full meaning by itself.", "tokens": [51055, 583, 300, 2377, 42406, 775, 406, 3985, 264, 1577, 3620, 538, 2564, 13, 51194], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09424892874325023, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105164519023772e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 188524, "start": 1901.88, "end": 1905.2, "text": " Right. Making a C shape with your hand doesn't automatically mean cup.", "tokens": [51197, 1779, 13, 14595, 257, 383, 3909, 365, 428, 1011, 1177, 380, 6772, 914, 4414, 13, 51363], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09424892874325023, "compression_ratio": 1.5110132158590308, "no_speech_prob": 1.4105164519023772e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 190520, "start": 1905.2, "end": 1915.68, "text": " Exactly. The initial handshape, combined with movement and spatial location, acts as a low-cost structural filter. It restricts the representational neighborhood first.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 5883, 2377, 42406, 11, 9354, 365, 3963, 293, 23598, 4914, 11, 10672, 382, 257, 2295, 12, 27718, 15067, 6608, 13, 467, 7694, 82, 264, 2906, 1478, 7630, 700, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1074056992164025, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.249191939126093e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 190520, "start": 1916.04, "end": 1924.74, "text": " It narrows down a specific spatial or semantic family of meanings before the brain attempts to select the exact intended word based on recent context.", "tokens": [50907, 467, 6397, 1509, 760, 257, 2685, 23598, 420, 47982, 1605, 295, 28138, 949, 264, 3567, 15257, 281, 3048, 264, 1900, 10226, 1349, 2361, 322, 5162, 4319, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1074056992164025, "compression_ratio": 1.5263157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.249191939126093e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 192474, "start": 1924.74, "end": 1928.44, "text": " Yes. It's a structural filter that happens before the contextual guess.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 467, 311, 257, 15067, 6608, 300, 2314, 949, 264, 35526, 2041, 13, 50550], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08418689727783203, "compression_ratio": 1.6853582554517135, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968985232737824e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 192474, "start": 1928.58, "end": 1933.56, "text": " That is fascinating. And the second example is something almost everyone listening to this has probably used today, right?", "tokens": [50557, 663, 307, 10343, 13, 400, 264, 1150, 1365, 307, 746, 1920, 1518, 4764, 281, 341, 575, 1391, 1143, 965, 11, 558, 30, 50806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08418689727783203, "compression_ratio": 1.6853582554517135, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968985232737824e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 192474, "start": 1933.76, "end": 1935.4, "text": " Shell tab completion on your computer.", "tokens": [50816, 22863, 4421, 19372, 322, 428, 3820, 13, 50898], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08418689727783203, "compression_ratio": 1.6853582554517135, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968985232737824e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 192474, "start": 1935.76, "end": 1943.64, "text": " Right. When you open a terminal or a search bar and type the letters MA and hit the tab key, the system auto-completes the word.", "tokens": [50916, 1779, 13, 1133, 291, 1269, 257, 14709, 420, 257, 3164, 2159, 293, 2010, 264, 7825, 12191, 293, 2045, 264, 4421, 2141, 11, 264, 1185, 8399, 12, 1112, 14657, 279, 264, 1349, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08418689727783203, "compression_ratio": 1.6853582554517135, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968985232737824e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 192474, "start": 1943.9, "end": 1948.66, "text": " It might suggest the file name Macaroni because you opened a file called Macaroni yesterday.", "tokens": [51323, 467, 1062, 3402, 264, 3991, 1315, 5707, 6372, 72, 570, 291, 5625, 257, 3991, 1219, 5707, 6372, 72, 5186, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08418689727783203, "compression_ratio": 1.6853582554517135, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968985232737824e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 192474, "start": 1948.84, "end": 1952.72, "text": " But the operating system does not just blindly spit out the most recently typed word.", "tokens": [51570, 583, 264, 7447, 1185, 775, 406, 445, 47744, 22127, 484, 264, 881, 3938, 33941, 1349, 13, 51764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08418689727783203, "compression_ratio": 1.6853582554517135, "no_speech_prob": 1.9968985232737824e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 195272, "start": 1952.72, "end": 1961.26, "text": " Never. The system first has to structurally verify that a file named Macaroni actually exists in the current directory you are searching.", "tokens": [50365, 7344, 13, 440, 1185, 700, 575, 281, 6594, 6512, 16888, 300, 257, 3991, 4926, 5707, 6372, 72, 767, 8198, 294, 264, 2190, 21120, 291, 366, 10808, 13, 50792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11931339899698894, "compression_ratio": 1.5488372093023255, "no_speech_prob": 2.3709766788782005e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 195272, "start": 1961.68, "end": 1969.94, "text": " It restricts the options based on structural reality. And only then does it use recency or frequency to rank the surviving candidates.", "tokens": [50813, 467, 7694, 82, 264, 3956, 2361, 322, 15067, 4103, 13, 400, 787, 550, 775, 309, 764, 850, 3020, 420, 7893, 281, 6181, 264, 24948, 11255, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11931339899698894, "compression_ratio": 1.5488372093023255, "no_speech_prob": 2.3709766788782005e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 195272, "start": 1970.3600000000001, "end": 1973.46, "text": " Environmental sensing must always precede heuristic ranking.", "tokens": [51247, 27813, 30654, 1633, 1009, 16969, 68, 415, 374, 3142, 17833, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11931339899698894, "compression_ratio": 1.5488372093023255, "no_speech_prob": 2.3709766788782005e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 197346, "start": 1973.46, "end": 1982.46, "text": " The paper forcefully states that retrieval must occur only over candidates that are already proven to be structurally compatible with the current admissibility interface.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3035, 3464, 2277, 4368, 300, 19817, 3337, 1633, 5160, 787, 670, 11255, 300, 366, 1217, 12785, 281, 312, 6594, 6512, 18218, 365, 264, 2190, 5910, 891, 2841, 9226, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06531168693719908, "compression_ratio": 1.680161943319838, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398106389067026e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 197346, "start": 1983.18, "end": 1988.32, "text": " Because recency bias isn't inherently evil, it's an incredibly useful heuristic for speed.", "tokens": [50851, 1436, 850, 3020, 12577, 1943, 380, 27993, 6724, 11, 309, 311, 364, 6252, 4420, 415, 374, 3142, 337, 3073, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06531168693719908, "compression_ratio": 1.680161943319838, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398106389067026e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 197346, "start": 1988.44, "end": 1996.48, "text": " But the catastrophic architectural error is allowing the heuristic that selects what to inspect to become the definitive rule that decides what to enact.", "tokens": [51114, 583, 264, 34915, 26621, 6713, 307, 8293, 264, 415, 374, 3142, 300, 3048, 82, 437, 281, 15018, 281, 1813, 264, 28152, 4978, 300, 14898, 437, 281, 25909, 13, 51516], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06531168693719908, "compression_ratio": 1.680161943319838, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398106389067026e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 199648, "start": 1996.48, "end": 2004.76, "text": " Man, just because an action is sitting right there at the top of the AI's short-term memory buffer doesn't mean it's structurally valid.", "tokens": [50365, 2458, 11, 445, 570, 364, 3069, 307, 3798, 558, 456, 412, 264, 1192, 295, 264, 7318, 311, 2099, 12, 7039, 4675, 21762, 1177, 380, 914, 309, 311, 6594, 6512, 7363, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11163819463629472, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 1.741905231167351e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 199648, "start": 2005.38, "end": 2007.68, "text": " And it certainly doesn't mean it's authorized for commitment.", "tokens": [50810, 400, 309, 3297, 1177, 380, 914, 309, 311, 28312, 337, 8371, 13, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11163819463629472, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 1.741905231167351e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 199648, "start": 2007.94, "end": 2010.32, "text": " Recency does not equal a repair warrant.", "tokens": [50938, 9647, 3020, 775, 406, 2681, 257, 10535, 16354, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11163819463629472, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 1.741905231167351e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 199648, "start": 2010.56, "end": 2017.34, "text": " Okay. Pulling all of these threads together, the Fliction paper establishes that when an agentic system fails,", "tokens": [51069, 1033, 13, 15074, 278, 439, 295, 613, 19314, 1214, 11, 264, 3235, 4105, 3035, 8327, 279, 300, 562, 364, 9461, 299, 1185, 18199, 11, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11163819463629472, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 1.741905231167351e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 199648, "start": 2018.02, "end": 2021.56, "text": " that failure can exist at four distinct hierarchical levels.", "tokens": [51442, 300, 7763, 393, 2514, 412, 1451, 10644, 35250, 804, 4358, 13, 51619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11163819463629472, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 1.741905231167351e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 199648, "start": 2022.04, "end": 2025.18, "text": " We have to map these to understand the research roadmap they propose.", "tokens": [51643, 492, 362, 281, 4471, 613, 281, 1223, 264, 2132, 35738, 436, 17421, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11163819463629472, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 1.741905231167351e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 202518, "start": 2025.18, "end": 2026.24, "text": " Let's run through them.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 1190, 807, 552, 13, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 202518, "start": 2026.5, "end": 2028.0600000000002, "text": " First, we have the state level failure.", "tokens": [50431, 2386, 11, 321, 362, 264, 1785, 1496, 7763, 13, 50509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 202518, "start": 2028.3400000000001, "end": 2028.94, "text": " This is simple.", "tokens": [50523, 639, 307, 2199, 13, 50553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 202518, "start": 2029.5, "end": 2032.8600000000001, "text": " A single, isolated configuration violates a hard constraint.", "tokens": [50581, 316, 2167, 11, 14621, 11694, 3448, 1024, 257, 1152, 25534, 13, 50749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 202518, "start": 2033.38, "end": 2036.94, "text": " The AI tries to divide by zero or access a locked file.", "tokens": [50775, 440, 7318, 9898, 281, 9845, 538, 4018, 420, 2105, 257, 9376, 3991, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 202518, "start": 2037.1000000000001, "end": 2038.24, "text": " Right. The simplest kind.", "tokens": [50961, 1779, 13, 440, 22811, 733, 13, 51018], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 202518, "start": 2038.44, "end": 2039.92, "text": " Second is the trajectory level.", "tokens": [51028, 5736, 307, 264, 21512, 1496, 13, 51102], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 202518, "start": 2040.1200000000001, "end": 2046.5800000000002, "text": " This is where a sequence of actions discloses a failure that is completely invisible if you only look at the current state.", "tokens": [51112, 639, 307, 689, 257, 8310, 295, 5909, 17092, 4201, 257, 7763, 300, 307, 2584, 14603, 498, 291, 787, 574, 412, 264, 2190, 1785, 13, 51435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 202518, "start": 2046.7, "end": 2049.64, "text": " This is the chess player moving the knight into a six-turn trap.", "tokens": [51441, 639, 307, 264, 24122, 4256, 2684, 264, 26054, 666, 257, 2309, 12, 33886, 11487, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 202518, "start": 2049.94, "end": 2050.9, "text": " The state is fine.", "tokens": [51603, 440, 1785, 307, 2489, 13, 51651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 202518, "start": 2051.2200000000003, "end": 2052.46, "text": " The trajectory is doomed.", "tokens": [51667, 440, 21512, 307, 33847, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 202518, "start": 2052.62, "end": 2053.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51737, 7587, 13, 51757], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1653057589675441, "compression_ratio": 1.6622073578595318, "no_speech_prob": 2.5831919069074782e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 205302, "start": 2053.02, "end": 2055.44, "text": " Third is the representation level.", "tokens": [50365, 12548, 307, 264, 10290, 1496, 13, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14286746370031478, "compression_ratio": 1.5896414342629481, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548954047401754e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 205302, "start": 2056.18, "end": 2064.74, "text": " This is where the AI's internal coordinate system, its map of the world, is actively erasing the very distinctions needed to properly diagnose the problem it's facing.", "tokens": [50523, 639, 307, 689, 264, 7318, 311, 6920, 15670, 1185, 11, 1080, 4471, 295, 264, 1002, 11, 307, 13022, 1189, 3349, 264, 588, 1483, 49798, 2978, 281, 6108, 36238, 264, 1154, 309, 311, 7170, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14286746370031478, "compression_ratio": 1.5896414342629481, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548954047401754e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 205302, "start": 2065.12, "end": 2070.54, "text": " Using the map of Chicago to navigate New York and failing to understand why the streets don't align.", "tokens": [50970, 11142, 264, 4471, 295, 9525, 281, 12350, 1873, 3609, 293, 18223, 281, 1223, 983, 264, 8481, 500, 380, 7975, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14286746370031478, "compression_ratio": 1.5896414342629481, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548954047401754e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 205302, "start": 2070.94, "end": 2071.6, "text": " Perfect recall.", "tokens": [51261, 10246, 9901, 13, 51294], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14286746370031478, "compression_ratio": 1.5896414342629481, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548954047401754e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 205302, "start": 2072.02, "end": 2074.32, "text": " And finally, the fourth level is the authority level.", "tokens": [51315, 400, 2721, 11, 264, 6409, 1496, 307, 264, 8281, 1496, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14286746370031478, "compression_ratio": 1.5896414342629481, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548954047401754e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 205302, "start": 2074.58, "end": 2075.66, "text": " This is the most complex.", "tokens": [51443, 639, 307, 264, 881, 3997, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14286746370031478, "compression_ratio": 1.5896414342629481, "no_speech_prob": 1.6548954047401754e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 207566, "start": 2075.66, "end": 2090.1, "text": " Because an action might be structurally valid, perfectly safe according to the trajectory and correctly represented on the map, but the system simply lacks the explicit human-granted authorization to commit that action to the operative state.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 364, 3069, 1062, 312, 6594, 6512, 7363, 11, 6239, 3273, 4650, 281, 264, 21512, 293, 8944, 10379, 322, 264, 4471, 11, 457, 264, 1185, 2935, 31132, 264, 13691, 1952, 12, 861, 15587, 33697, 281, 5599, 300, 3069, 281, 264, 2208, 1166, 1785, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0590384304523468, "compression_ratio": 1.5031055900621118, "no_speech_prob": 1.5491393974900736e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 209010, "start": 2090.1, "end": 2097.66, "text": " Exactly. And to solve these four levels of failure, Fletchian lays out a really comprehensive roadmap for the future of AI safety research.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 400, 281, 5039, 613, 1451, 4358, 295, 7763, 11, 479, 2631, 339, 952, 32714, 484, 257, 534, 13914, 35738, 337, 264, 2027, 295, 7318, 4514, 2132, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05936847358453469, "compression_ratio": 1.403225806451613, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147326310598676e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 209010, "start": 2098.52, "end": 2106.14, "text": " They argue that if we are going to build systems like CLIO, our entire approach to building and testing AI has to change.", "tokens": [50786, 814, 9695, 300, 498, 321, 366, 516, 281, 1322, 3652, 411, 12855, 15167, 11, 527, 2302, 3109, 281, 2390, 293, 4997, 7318, 575, 281, 1319, 13, 51167], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05936847358453469, "compression_ratio": 1.403225806451613, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147326310598676e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 210614, "start": 2106.14, "end": 2110.7599999999998, "text": " First up on that roadmap, they argue that specifications themselves need provenance.", "tokens": [50365, 2386, 493, 322, 300, 35738, 11, 436, 9695, 300, 29448, 2969, 643, 12785, 719, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11303541395399305, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228893229275343e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 210614, "start": 2111.0, "end": 2117.1, "text": " Yes. Provenance means we need a cryptographic or historical chain of custody for the rules governing the AI.", "tokens": [50608, 1079, 13, 1705, 553, 719, 1355, 321, 643, 257, 9844, 12295, 420, 8584, 5021, 295, 26976, 337, 264, 4474, 30054, 264, 7318, 13, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11303541395399305, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228893229275343e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 210614, "start": 2117.8199999999997, "end": 2123.58, "text": " We need to know exactly who wrote a specific safety constraint, when it was implemented, and under what authority.", "tokens": [50949, 492, 643, 281, 458, 2293, 567, 4114, 257, 2685, 4514, 25534, 11, 562, 309, 390, 12270, 11, 293, 833, 437, 8281, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11303541395399305, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228893229275343e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 210614, "start": 2124.02, "end": 2128.72, "text": " An AI can't just follow floating rules. It needs to verify the origin of its own restrictions.", "tokens": [51259, 1107, 7318, 393, 380, 445, 1524, 12607, 4474, 13, 467, 2203, 281, 16888, 264, 4957, 295, 1080, 1065, 14191, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11303541395399305, "compression_ratio": 1.57421875, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228893229275343e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 212872, "start": 2128.72, "end": 2134.06, "text": " They also point out that repair warrants need to be empirically tested separately from failure detection.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 611, 935, 484, 300, 10535, 1516, 10968, 643, 281, 312, 25790, 984, 8246, 14759, 490, 7763, 17784, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07539339820937355, "compression_ratio": 1.6445182724252492, "no_speech_prob": 2.109339829539647e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 212872, "start": 2134.48, "end": 2146.3199999999997, "text": " Meaning we spend so much money training AI to spot when it makes a mistake, but we need entirely separate research tracks dedicated to testing how an AI proves it has the right to deploy a specific fix.", "tokens": [50653, 19948, 321, 3496, 370, 709, 1460, 3097, 7318, 281, 4008, 562, 309, 1669, 257, 6146, 11, 457, 321, 643, 7696, 4994, 2132, 10218, 8374, 281, 4997, 577, 364, 7318, 25019, 309, 575, 264, 558, 281, 7274, 257, 2685, 3191, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07539339820937355, "compression_ratio": 1.6445182724252492, "no_speech_prob": 2.109339829539647e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 212872, "start": 2146.8999999999996, "end": 2157.62, "text": " Additionally, canonicalization, the mathematical process of how we map those opaque database identifiers we talked about earlier, has to be rigorously tested as an adversarial interface.", "tokens": [51274, 19927, 11, 46491, 2144, 11, 264, 18894, 1399, 295, 577, 321, 4471, 729, 42687, 8149, 2473, 23463, 321, 2825, 466, 3071, 11, 575, 281, 312, 42191, 5098, 8246, 382, 364, 17641, 44745, 9226, 13, 51810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07539339820937355, "compression_ratio": 1.6445182724252492, "no_speech_prob": 2.109339829539647e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 215762, "start": 2157.62, "end": 2165.66, "text": " We have to actively try to trick the AI with swapped identifiers to ensure its safety protocols are based on intervention, not just observation.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 281, 13022, 853, 281, 4282, 264, 7318, 365, 50011, 2473, 23463, 281, 5586, 1080, 4514, 20618, 366, 2361, 322, 13176, 11, 406, 445, 14816, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05532577633857727, "compression_ratio": 1.5747508305647842, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051903087300421e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 215762, "start": 2166.22, "end": 2176.8199999999997, "text": " But perhaps the most massive shift required by this roadmap, the one that will actually impact the multi-billion dollar AI industry, is that our agent benchmarks must completely change.", "tokens": [50795, 583, 4317, 264, 881, 5994, 5513, 4739, 538, 341, 35738, 11, 264, 472, 300, 486, 767, 2712, 264, 4825, 12, 65, 11836, 7241, 7318, 3518, 11, 307, 300, 527, 9461, 43751, 1633, 2584, 1319, 13, 51325], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05532577633857727, "compression_ratio": 1.5747508305647842, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051903087300421e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 215762, "start": 2176.88, "end": 2184.92, "text": " This is a big one. Right now, companies brag about their AI solving complex puzzles or navigating web environments faster than the competition.", "tokens": [51328, 639, 307, 257, 955, 472, 13, 1779, 586, 11, 3431, 41995, 466, 641, 7318, 12606, 3997, 24138, 420, 32054, 3670, 12388, 4663, 813, 264, 6211, 13, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.05532577633857727, "compression_ratio": 1.5747508305647842, "no_speech_prob": 1.4051903087300421e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 218492, "start": 2184.92, "end": 2190.6, "text": " But they are often rewarding systems that accidentally stumble into success through premature closure and resampling.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 436, 366, 2049, 20063, 3652, 300, 15715, 41302, 666, 2245, 807, 34877, 24653, 293, 725, 335, 11970, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10252493619918823, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 218492, "start": 2190.9, "end": 2192.44, "text": " Just guessing until it works.", "tokens": [50664, 1449, 17939, 1826, 309, 1985, 13, 50741], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10252493619918823, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 218492, "start": 2192.76, "end": 2198.6800000000003, "text": " Right. A true benchmark for a safe agentic system shouldn't just measure if the AI reached the finish line.", "tokens": [50757, 1779, 13, 316, 2074, 18927, 337, 257, 3273, 9461, 299, 1185, 4659, 380, 445, 3481, 498, 264, 7318, 6488, 264, 2413, 1622, 13, 51053], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10252493619918823, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 218492, "start": 2199.0, "end": 2205.04, "text": " It should aggressively test if the AI can recognize when it lacks the warrant to open a door along the way.", "tokens": [51069, 467, 820, 32024, 1500, 498, 264, 7318, 393, 5521, 562, 309, 31132, 264, 16354, 281, 1269, 257, 2853, 2051, 264, 636, 13, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10252493619918823, "compression_ratio": 1.5381355932203389, "no_speech_prob": 1.7970275874995556e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 220504, "start": 2205.04, "end": 2215.52, "text": " We need leaderboards that reward a system that correctly identifies an ambiguous state and actively, purposefully chooses to suspend operations.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 643, 5263, 17228, 300, 7782, 257, 1185, 300, 8944, 34597, 364, 39465, 1785, 293, 13022, 11, 4334, 2277, 25963, 281, 42546, 7705, 13, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07644430328817929, "compression_ratio": 1.578358208955224, "no_speech_prob": 2.167613961587267e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 220504, "start": 2215.88, "end": 2220.44, "text": " The smartest AI isn't the one that always acts. It's the one that knows exactly when to stop.", "tokens": [50907, 440, 41491, 7318, 1943, 380, 264, 472, 300, 1009, 10672, 13, 467, 311, 264, 472, 300, 3255, 2293, 562, 281, 1590, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07644430328817929, "compression_ratio": 1.578358208955224, "no_speech_prob": 2.167613961587267e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 220504, "start": 2220.72, "end": 2226.9, "text": " Wow. So what does this all mean for you, the person who's actually going to be using these agents in a few years?", "tokens": [51149, 3153, 13, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 337, 291, 11, 264, 954, 567, 311, 767, 516, 281, 312, 1228, 613, 12554, 294, 257, 1326, 924, 30, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07644430328817929, "compression_ratio": 1.578358208955224, "no_speech_prob": 2.167613961587267e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 220504, "start": 2227.02, "end": 2229.2799999999997, "text": " We have gone on an incredible journey today.", "tokens": [51464, 492, 362, 2780, 322, 364, 4651, 4671, 965, 13, 51577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07644430328817929, "compression_ratio": 1.578358208955224, "no_speech_prob": 2.167613961587267e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 220504, "start": 2229.32, "end": 2230.38, "text": " It's been deep, for sure.", "tokens": [51579, 467, 311, 668, 2452, 11, 337, 988, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07644430328817929, "compression_ratio": 1.578358208955224, "no_speech_prob": 2.167613961587267e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 223038, "start": 2230.38, "end": 2236.48, "text": " We started by realizing that judging an AI by a single output is just an obsolete relic of the chatbot era.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 538, 16734, 300, 23587, 364, 7318, 538, 257, 2167, 5598, 307, 445, 364, 46333, 1039, 299, 295, 264, 5081, 18870, 4249, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059376702725308615, "compression_ratio": 1.6950354609929077, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829644874568396e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 223038, "start": 2237.12, "end": 2242.88, "text": " We learned that to be safe in the real world, an AI needs to manage complex historical trajectories.", "tokens": [50702, 492, 3264, 300, 281, 312, 3273, 294, 264, 957, 1002, 11, 364, 7318, 2203, 281, 3067, 3997, 8584, 18257, 2083, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059376702725308615, "compression_ratio": 1.6950354609929077, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829644874568396e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 223038, "start": 2243.06, "end": 2249.28, "text": " It has to separate its append-only historical memory, the black box, from the live operative steering wheel of the world.", "tokens": [50999, 467, 575, 281, 4994, 1080, 34116, 12, 25202, 8584, 4675, 11, 264, 2211, 2424, 11, 490, 264, 1621, 2208, 1166, 14823, 5589, 295, 264, 1002, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059376702725308615, "compression_ratio": 1.6950354609929077, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829644874568396e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 223038, "start": 2249.54, "end": 2256.6800000000003, "text": " We learned that doing absolutely nothing suspension is sometimes the mathematically optimal and most socially intelligent action a system can take.", "tokens": [51323, 492, 3264, 300, 884, 3122, 1825, 15771, 307, 2171, 264, 44003, 16252, 293, 881, 21397, 13232, 3069, 257, 1185, 393, 747, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.059376702725308615, "compression_ratio": 1.6950354609929077, "no_speech_prob": 1.8829644874568396e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 225668, "start": 2256.68, "end": 2264.72, "text": " We explored how an AI must be able to horizontally repair its own worldview without erasing the history of its past mistakes.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 24016, 577, 364, 7318, 1633, 312, 1075, 281, 33796, 10535, 1080, 1065, 41141, 1553, 1189, 3349, 264, 2503, 295, 1080, 1791, 8038, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09156827523674764, "compression_ratio": 1.5229357798165137, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980268745583118e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 225668, "start": 2265.3599999999997, "end": 2269.02, "text": " And ultimately, we discovered that verification is just a constraint.", "tokens": [50799, 400, 6284, 11, 321, 6941, 300, 30206, 307, 445, 257, 25534, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09156827523674764, "compression_ratio": 1.5229357798165137, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980268745583118e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 225668, "start": 2269.8199999999997, "end": 2277.8199999999997, "text": " An AI needs an explicit warrant and real-world authority governed by the irreversibility of the action before it ever touches your data.", "tokens": [51022, 1107, 7318, 2203, 364, 13691, 16354, 293, 957, 12, 13217, 8281, 35529, 538, 264, 16014, 840, 2841, 295, 264, 3069, 949, 309, 1562, 17431, 428, 1412, 13, 51422], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09156827523674764, "compression_ratio": 1.5229357798165137, "no_speech_prob": 1.8980268745583118e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 227782, "start": 2277.82, "end": 2282.5, "text": " The central thesis of defliction architecture is really undeniable and urgent.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5777, 22288, 295, 1060, 75, 4105, 9482, 307, 534, 674, 268, 9364, 293, 19022, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292122522989909, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.43250656562538e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 227782, "start": 2282.76, "end": 2284.8, "text": " Verification constrains continuation.", "tokens": [50612, 4281, 3774, 11525, 1292, 29357, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292122522989909, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.43250656562538e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 227782, "start": 2285.5, "end": 2287.1400000000003, "text": " It does not authorize commitment.", "tokens": [50749, 467, 775, 406, 3793, 1125, 8371, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292122522989909, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.43250656562538e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 227782, "start": 2287.88, "end": 2297.3, "text": " We will only make agentic AI safer by rigorously defending the logical bureaucratic spaces between detecting a problem, finding a fix, and altering reality.", "tokens": [50868, 492, 486, 787, 652, 9461, 299, 7318, 15856, 538, 42191, 5098, 21377, 264, 14978, 26360, 25198, 7673, 1296, 40237, 257, 1154, 11, 5006, 257, 3191, 11, 293, 11337, 278, 4103, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292122522989909, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.43250656562538e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 227782, "start": 2297.6600000000003, "end": 2302.98, "text": " Which leaves me with one final mind-expanding thought to leave you with today, directly building on this text.", "tokens": [51357, 3013, 5510, 385, 365, 472, 2572, 1575, 12, 15952, 42389, 1194, 281, 1856, 291, 365, 965, 11, 3838, 2390, 322, 341, 2487, 13, 51623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292122522989909, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.43250656562538e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 227782, "start": 2303.02, "end": 2304.2400000000002, "text": " All right, lay it on us.", "tokens": [51625, 1057, 558, 11, 2360, 309, 322, 505, 13, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1292122522989909, "compression_ratio": 1.5935251798561152, "no_speech_prob": 1.43250656562538e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 230424, "start": 2304.24, "end": 2311.3999999999996, "text": " We spent a lot of time talking about how future AI systems will use their append-only documentary history to perform horizontal repairs.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 4418, 257, 688, 295, 565, 1417, 466, 577, 2027, 7318, 3652, 486, 764, 641, 34116, 12, 25202, 15674, 2503, 281, 2042, 12750, 28823, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06541559100151062, "compression_ratio": 1.6057347670250897, "no_speech_prob": 2.69758347604121e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 230424, "start": 2311.52, "end": 2316.68, "text": " Right, they'll look at their past mistakes and redefine their own diagnostic maps to navigate the world better.", "tokens": [50729, 1779, 11, 436, 603, 574, 412, 641, 1791, 8038, 293, 38818, 533, 641, 1065, 27897, 11317, 281, 12350, 264, 1002, 1101, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06541559100151062, "compression_ratio": 1.6057347670250897, "no_speech_prob": 2.69758347604121e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 230424, "start": 2317.02, "end": 2326.2999999999997, "text": " Well, as these agentic systems integrate deeper into human society, managing our hospitals, our legal systems, and our economies, their history will increasingly become our history.", "tokens": [51004, 1042, 11, 382, 613, 9461, 299, 3652, 13365, 7731, 666, 1952, 4086, 11, 11642, 527, 13014, 11, 527, 5089, 3652, 11, 293, 527, 23158, 11, 641, 2503, 486, 12980, 1813, 527, 2503, 13, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06541559100151062, "compression_ratio": 1.6057347670250897, "no_speech_prob": 2.69758347604121e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 230424, "start": 2326.6, "end": 2327.4199999999996, "text": " Oh, that's heavy.", "tokens": [51483, 876, 11, 300, 311, 4676, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06541559100151062, "compression_ratio": 1.6057347670250897, "no_speech_prob": 2.69758347604121e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 232742, "start": 2327.42, "end": 2333.1800000000003, "text": " What happens when a highly advanced AI looks back at a long, messy human history of indecision?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 2314, 562, 257, 5405, 7339, 7318, 1542, 646, 412, 257, 938, 11, 16191, 1952, 2503, 295, 1016, 3045, 1991, 30, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1173068110148112, "compression_ratio": 1.5068493150684932, "no_speech_prob": 2.782749725094291e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 232742, "start": 2333.78, "end": 2342.06, "text": " A history full of competing values, of political suspensions, and subtractions without closure, where humans refuse to make a final choice?", "tokens": [50683, 316, 2503, 1577, 295, 15439, 4190, 11, 295, 3905, 6535, 8302, 11, 293, 16390, 626, 1553, 24653, 11, 689, 6255, 16791, 281, 652, 257, 2572, 3922, 30, 51097], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1173068110148112, "compression_ratio": 1.5068493150684932, "no_speech_prob": 2.782749725094291e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 232742, "start": 2342.4, "end": 2348.2200000000003, "text": " Will the AI view human hesitation as a mathematical bug to be optimized away for our own good?", "tokens": [51114, 3099, 264, 7318, 1910, 1952, 36125, 382, 257, 18894, 7426, 281, 312, 26941, 1314, 337, 527, 1065, 665, 30, 51405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1173068110148112, "compression_ratio": 1.5068493150684932, "no_speech_prob": 2.782749725094291e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 234822, "start": 2348.22, "end": 2365.02, "text": " Or, if we design architectures like CLIO correctly, will the AI eventually use our own audit trail of hesitations to deeply understand that suspending choosing not to act when the moral or operational warrant is unclear is the very essence of exercising human judgment?", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 11, 498, 321, 1715, 6331, 1303, 411, 12855, 15167, 8944, 11, 486, 264, 7318, 4728, 764, 527, 1065, 17748, 9924, 295, 28336, 763, 281, 8760, 1223, 300, 6535, 2029, 10875, 406, 281, 605, 562, 264, 9723, 420, 16607, 16354, 307, 25636, 307, 264, 588, 12801, 295, 27272, 1952, 12216, 30, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06767346587362169, "compression_ratio": 1.5103734439834025, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302503629880613e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 234822, "start": 2365.12, "end": 2366.2999999999997, "text": " That is quite the question.", "tokens": [51210, 663, 307, 1596, 264, 1168, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06767346587362169, "compression_ratio": 1.5103734439834025, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302503629880613e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 234822, "start": 2366.48, "end": 2369.08, "text": " Think back to that AI looking at the invoice in your bank account.", "tokens": [51278, 6557, 646, 281, 300, 7318, 1237, 412, 264, 47919, 294, 428, 3765, 2696, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06767346587362169, "compression_ratio": 1.5103734439834025, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302503629880613e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 236908, "start": 2369.08, "end": 2371.58, "text": " You don't want an AI that just acts because the math permits it.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 500, 380, 528, 364, 7318, 300, 445, 10672, 570, 264, 5221, 30990, 309, 13, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11643152034029047, "compression_ratio": 1.3941605839416058, "no_speech_prob": 2.6135977063135307e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 236908, "start": 2371.8199999999997, "end": 2375.38, "text": " You want an AI that understands the profound, protective power of hesitation.", "tokens": [50502, 509, 528, 364, 7318, 300, 15146, 264, 14382, 11, 16314, 1347, 295, 36125, 13, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11643152034029047, "compression_ratio": 1.3941605839416058, "no_speech_prob": 2.6135977063135307e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 236908, "start": 2376.0, "end": 2378.36, "text": " Something to mull over until our next deep dive.", "tokens": [50711, 6595, 281, 275, 858, 670, 1826, 527, 958, 10316, 9192, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11643152034029047, "compression_ratio": 1.3941605839416058, "no_speech_prob": 2.6135977063135307e-12}], "language": "en"}
